tep-finish", "tokens": {"total": 129141, "input": 1219, "output": 178, "reasoning": 0, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 127744}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_13663da99001vbf8N1NcXJ8m9s", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13663c3c5002JKnZX803aQOpF2"}]}, {"info": {"parentID": "msg_136627b83001E1n21s9P65Wy1w", "role": "assistant", "mode": "build", "agent": "build", "path": {"cwd": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code", "root": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"total": 130884, "input": 897, "output": 234, "reasoning": 857, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 128896}}, "modelID": "big-pickle", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1791913877165, "completed": 1791913893782}, "finish": "tool-calls", "id": "msg_13663dead002BnHhVsMzORkmbC", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_13663f06d001UxMara8Uj3r1o6", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13663dead002BnHhVsMzORkmbC"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "Now this is very informative. In the RELEASED v2.0.0 APK:\n- `classes4.dex` = **30,163,093** bytes (compressed) — this is the giant DEX containing the RuWordList strings! It's the largest entry. (Note: earlier `unzip -v` shows \"Length\" column 1 and \"Size\" column 3; my awk prints $3 = compressed size. So classes4.dex compressed = 30.16MB.)\n- Total compressed = 82.7MB (the 87MB includes zip central directory / signing block overhead ~4MB).\n\nSo the dictionary DEX (classes4.dex) is 30MB COMPRESSED in the release APK! Why so big compressed? Because DEX string data with 3M strings doesn't compress as well as raw concatenated text (interleaved offsets, ULEB lengths, null terminators, and possibly the strings are not contiguous — DEX string_data section may order strings and have entropy). Actually the compressed 30MB for ~86MB uncompressed = 2.9:1, worse than our gzip 8.8MB for 68MB text (7.7:1). The difference: DEX layout breaks long runs, and R8 might not have removed anything.\n\nWait — but is classes4.dex ONLY the dictionary? 30MB compressed for strings that as plain gzipped text are 8.8MB. The DEX overhead + poor layout inflates it ~3.4x. Regardless, in the RELEASE APK the dictionary effectively costs ~30MB!\n\nSo replacing it with an 11.3MB compressed asset saves ~30 - 11.3 = **~19MB** in the APK. New release APK ≈ 87 - 19 ≈ 68MB. That's meaningful but maybe not enough for the failing device.\n\nBut wait — why is classes4.dex 30MB compressed when the raw text gzips to 8.8MB? Let me verify classes4.dex is the dict. It's plausible R8 put the 3M strings there. The compression delta is suspicious but DEX string data has lots of structure. Also maybe the strings are uppercase+lowercase? No, only lowercase in source; but Kotlin compiler may intern. Hmm.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: maybe classes4.dex contains the array construction code `arrayOf(...)` in 603 functions. `arrayOf` of 3M strings creates bytecode with 3M `const-string` instructions (each referencing a string index) + array fills. R8 might keep the methods. The code is large. Also string_data section. So 30MB compressed.\n\nAnyway, the empirical fix: remove classes4.dex (30MB) → add asset (11.3MB) → save ~19MB. New release ~68MB.\n\nIs 68MB enough? The failing device had 0 allocatable when needing 87MB. We don't know its total free space. If it had, say, 70MB free, 68MB might just fit (needs ~68MB + staging overhead). If it had 40MB free, still fails.\n\nHmm, but this is a big improvement (87→68, -22%). Combined with the fact that debug APK also dropped? Let me verify by building the new release. Actually, I can estimate more precisely from the debug comparison: debug old would have had classes.dex with the strings. But I deleted the .kt; I can't build old easily. But I have the released old APK. Let me build new release and compare directly.\n\nBefore building, let me double check classes4.dex content by extracting and looking at strings — confirm it's the wordlist. Let me grep the dex for a known word \"АБДУЛАХАДОВИЧАМ\". Actually compressed dex inside zip; `unzip -p ... classes4.dex | strings | grep`. Let me verify.\n\nLet me confirm classes4.dex holds the dictionary.", "time": {"start": 1791913881781, "end": 1791913887780}, "id": "prt_13663f0b5001TeA4CjO05sfuzo", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13663dead002BnHhVsMzORkmbC"}, {"type": "text", "text": "`classes4.dex` = 30 МБ (сжатый) — вот он, словарь. Проверю, что это именно он, и посчитаю реальный выигрыш.", "time": {"start": 1791913887786, "end": 1791913888860}, "id": "prt_13664082a001rmRur2btaXNeD8", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13663dead002BnHhVsMzORkmbC"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "bash", "callID": "call_00_yshwsx42znxru7m5x57291xh", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"command": "cd /tmp/opencode && unzip -p yomikai-v2.0.0.apk classes4.dex 2>/dev/null | strings | grep -c -i \"абдулахадович\\|КАКЖЕ\\|БАСКЕРВИЛЬ\" ; echo \"--- sample ---\"; unzip -p yomikai-v2.0.0.apk classes4.dex 2>/dev/null | strings | grep -i \"баскервиль\\|абдулахадович\" | head -3; echo \"--- dex compressed size ---\"; unzip -v yomikai-v2.0.0.apk 2>/dev/null | grep -E \"classes4.dex\""}, "output": "0\n--- sample ---\n--- dex compressed size ---\n140804312  Defl:N 30163093  79% 1981-01-01 01:01 3daa854a  classes4.dex\n", "metadata": {"output": "0\n--- sample ---\n--- dex compressed size ---\n140804312  Defl:N 30163093  79% 1981-01-01 01:01 3daa854a  classes4.dex\n", "exit": 0, "truncated": false}, "title": "cd /tmp/opencode && unzip -p yomikai-v2.0.0.apk classes4.dex 2>/dev/null | strings | grep -c -i \"абдулахадович\\|КАКЖЕ\\|БАСКЕРВИЛЬ\" ; echo \"--- sample ---\"; unzip -p yomikai-v2.0.0.apk classes4.dex 2>/dev/null | strings | grep -i \"баскервиль\\|абдулахадович\" | head -3; echo \"--- dex compressed size ---\"; unzip -v yomikai-v2.0.0.apk 2>/dev/null | grep -E \"classes4.dex\"", "time": {"start": 1791913888801, "end": 1791913893556}}, "id": "prt_1366409270011lGCCrzTTyDzON", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13663dead002BnHhVsMzORkmbC"}, {"reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-finish", "tokens": {"total": 130884, "input": 897, "output": 234, "reasoning": 857, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 128896}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_136641f1d0014Vjb3wQZQAWBTj", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13663dead002BnHhVsMzORkmbC"}]}, {"info": {"parentID": "msg_136627b83001E1n21s9P65Wy1w", "role": "assistant", "mode": "build", "agent": "build", "path": {"cwd": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code", "root": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"total": 131637, "input": 1153, "output": 167, "reasoning": 525, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 129792}}, "modelID": "big-pickle", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1791913894351, "completed": 1791913905607}, "finish": "tool-calls", "id": "msg_1366421cf002D1DVIgEbV3RHCd", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_13664325e001pzHnUdBvt6imJU", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1366421cf002D1DVIgEbV3RHCd"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "Interesting! `classes4.dex` uncompressed = 140,804,312 bytes (~134MB!) compressed to 30.16MB. But grep for \"абдулахадович\" found 0. Because strings in DEX are MUTF-8 but maybe the words are lowercase (source was lowercase). I grepped case-insensitive for lowercase patterns too (\"абдулахадович\" lowercase). Got 0. Hmm. Maybe the strings are compressed in dex? No. Or maybe classes4.dex is something else (e.g., ML Kit models?), and the dictionary is spread across classes3.dex (4.4MB compressed) etc.\n\nWait, 140MB uncompressed dex! That's the giant one. It must contain the 3M strings. But `strings` didn't find \"абдулахадович\". Let me try other words, or check if dex strings are stored with different encoding. Actually DEX string_data is MUTF-8, `strings` should find ASCII/Cyrillic UTF-8 sequences. Unless the dex is further compressed (it's not, dex isn't internally compressed). Hmm.\n\nMaybe my `strings` grep failed because the words are uppercase in one dex and lowercase in another, and classes4 contains something else. Let me search across ALL dex for a rare word.\n\nLet me extract all dex and grep for \"баскервиль\" (case-insensitive) and \"БАСКЕРВИЛЬ\". Also try \"содержала\".\n\nLet me do a robust search: unzip -p each classes*.dex | grep -a -o -i \"баскервиль\" | head.\n\nActually, let me just search the whole APK binary for the word (compressed entries won't match, so need to decompress). Let me loop over dex files.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the RuWordList strings were **obfuscated/optimized away**?? No, they're used.\n\nLet me just check classes4 with `strings -n 6` for Cyrillic. Actually `strings` default only prints ASCII sequences (>=4 printable ASCII). Cyrillic UTF-8 bytes are non-ASCII → `strings` won't print them! That's why 0 matches. Need `strings -e` or just grep the raw bytes.\n\nSo grep raw: `unzip -p ... classes4.dex | grep -a -c \"баскервиль\"` (binary grep). Let me do that.", "time": {"start": 1791913898639, "end": 1791913902546}, "id": "prt_13664328f001NS3v3TJPw9tIbP", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1366421cf002D1DVIgEbV3RHCd"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "bash", "callID": "call_00_g9m7ultqqqypntlufxk7pg31", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"command": "cd /tmp/opencode && for d in classes4.dex classes3.dex classes2.dex classes.dex; do c=$(unzip -p yomikai-v2.0.0.apk $d 2>/dev/null | grep -a -c \"БАСКЕРВИЛЬ\"); echo \"$d: БАСКЕРВИЛЬ matches=$c\"; done; echo \"--- lowercase in classes4 ---\"; unzip -p yomikai-v2.0.0.apk classes4.dex 2>/dev/null | grep -a -c \"абдулахадович\""}, "output": "classes4.dex: БАСКЕРВИЛЬ matches=1\nclasses3.dex: БАСКЕРВИЛЬ matches=0\nclasses2.dex: БАСКЕРВИЛЬ matches=0\nclasses.dex: БАСКЕРВИЛЬ matches=0\n--- lowercase in classes4 ---\n1\n", "metadata": {"output": "classes4.dex: БАСКЕРВИЛЬ matches=1\nclasses3.dex: БАСКЕРВИЛЬ matches=0\nclasses2.dex: БАСКЕРВИЛЬ matches=0\nclasses.dex: БАСКЕРВИЛЬ matches=0\n--- lowercase in classes4 ---\n1\n", "exit": 0, "truncated": false}, "title": "cd /tmp/opencode && for d in classes4.dex classes3.dex classes2.dex classes.dex; do c=$(unzip -p yomikai-v2.0.0.apk $d 2>/dev/null | grep -a -c \"БАСКЕРВИЛЬ\"); echo \"$d: БАСКЕРВИЛЬ matches=$c\"; done; echo \"--- lowercase in classes4 ---\"; unzip -p yomikai-v2.0.0.apk classes4.dex 2>/dev/null | grep -a -c \"абдулахадович\"", "time": {"start": 1791913903337, "end": 1791913905466}}, "id": "prt_1366441d6001wtaTldBhAVUbVZ", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1366421cf002D1DVIgEbV3RHCd"}, {"reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-finish", "tokens": {"total": 131637, "input": 1153, "output": 167, "reasoning": 525, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 129792}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_136644d7e001ov655hYs0IkLXN", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1366421cf002D1DVIgEbV3RHCd"}]}, {"info": {"parentID": "msg_136627b83001E1n21s9P65Wy1w", "role": "assistant", "mode": "build", "agent": "build", "path": {"cwd": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code", "root": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "reasoning": 0, "cache": {"read": 0, "write": 0}}, "modelID": "big-pickle", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1791913906212, "completed": 1791914382576}, "error": {"name": "MessageAbortedError", "data": {"message": "Aborted"}}, "id": "msg_136645024002yMnyfYbpQ8Nin5", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_136645d96001FX9AS7yWURZl8L", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136645024002yMnyfYbpQ8Nin5"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "Confirmed: `classes4.dex` contains the dictionary (lowercase and uppercase via seeds; the forms are lowercase and uppercase built at runtime, but \"БАСКЕРВИЛЬ\" appears because SEEDS/regression tokens are uppercase in source? Actually the generator lowercases seeds; but there may be uppercase literals from BEFORE... anyway it contains it).\n\nSo classes4.dex: uncompressed 140.8MB → compressed 30.16MB. That's the dictionary DEX (plus array code). Our asset replaces it with 11.34MB compressed. Savings ≈ 30.16 - 11.34 = **18.8MB**.\n\nBut wait: the uncompressed 140.8MB is huge — 65MB of string bytes become 140MB dex? Because DEX string_data includes ULEB length + bytes, string_ids 4 bytes each, plus the `const-string` instructions in 603 methods (3M instructions × ~3 bytes) and array fill. So DEX inflates a lot. Compressed 30MB.\n\nNow new release APK ≈ 87.1 - 18.8 = **68.3MB**. That's a solid reduction (-22%). But is it enough? Unknown. The device that failed needs 68MB free now. It's better.\n\nHmm, but I should aim higher. The user said \"не устанавливается\" — if the device had e.g. 50MB free, 68MB still fails. But maybe the device had ~80MB and 87 failed; 68 would succeed.\n\nBut actually — there might be MORE low-hanging fruit. The big items: `libmlkit_google_ocr_pipeline.so` 11MB, LiteRt 5.4MB, libimagedecoder 5.1MB, tesseract 3.8MB, etc. Plus the mlkit-google-ocr-models assets. But the project depends on built-in OCR; removing ML Kit would degrade features. The user wants no degradation. So keep.\n\nSo the main win is the dictionary (18.8MB). Given our constraint (no functional/perf regression), that's the right change.\n\nActually, we can do better on the dictionary too: our asset compresses to 11.34MB. Could we compress more? Options:\n- Store a **gzip** file (gzip level 9 = 8.79MB) as asset, but then the APK would store it... if we name it `.gz`, AGP might store it compressed again (double) — no benefit, and runtime double-decompresses. If we ensure it's NOT recompressed (noCompress \"gz\"), APK stores 8.79MB and runtime gunzips once → 8.79MB in APK (vs 11.34MB for plain text). Saves another 2.5MB. But adds runtime gunzip (the user's speed concern). Net APK 68.3 - 2.5 = ~65.8MB.\n- Or build a more compact binary format (e.g., sorted words in UTF-8, no newlines, or front-coded). But gzip already captures most.\n\nGiven the user's \"don't degrade speed\" priority, the plain-text asset (no extra decompress step) is the safer choice. The 2.5MB difference is minor vs the 18.8MB. Stick with plain text.\n\nBut hold on — let me reconsider the runtime cost of the plain asset vs old DEX. In the old release, RuWordList.upper built a HashSet from 603 arrays of DEX strings (no I/O). New: read 71MB from asset (deflated in zip, inflated on the fly) + split lines + insert. The inflation of 71MB and 3M `readLine()` calls. That's the added cost. On device maybe 0.5-1.5s one-time on background thread. The user accepted this (\"если ничего по скорости не критично\"). It's one-time and off the main thread. Acceptable. And we removed 3M `uppercase()` calls, partially offsetting.\n\nNow, let me VERIFY the new release APK size by building it. That's the key deliverable. Build `:app:assembleRelease`.\n\nAlso I should double check the debug asset compressed 11.34MB, and release similar. Let's build release.\n\nAlso, note: the released APK has NO `assets/ocr/` obviously. Good.\n\nOne more consideration: the release build in CI uses `release.yml`/`release-universal.yml` — does the CI build via Gradle and does it include our asset automatically? Yes, asset is in the data module → merged.\n\nLet me build release now and measure. Might take ~15 min.\n\nActually — before that, do I even need the full release build? I have strong evidence: savings = old classes4.dex compressed (30.16MB) - new asset compressed (~11.3MB) ≈ 18.8MB. New release ≈ 68.3MB. But to be safe and give the user a real number, build it.\n\nLet me run assembleRelease. It may complain about signing (release signingConfig = debug.signingConfig, possibly null). Let's try.\n\nLet me also confirm the app's `noCompress` doesn't include our asset extension — it's .txt, compressed as seen (11.3MB). Good.\n\nRun release build.", "time": {"start": 1791913909692, "end": 1791913917814}, "id": "prt_136645dbc0018Qh7CTMHMwrk4l", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136645024002yMnyfYbpQ8Nin5"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Подтверждено: `classes4.dex` (словарь) — **140,8 МБ несжато / 30,16 МБ в APK**. Замена ассетом (11,3 МБ) должна срезать ~19 МБ. Собираю релиз для точного замера.", "time": {"start": 1791913917818, "end": 1791913918597}, "id": "prt_136647d7a001w85qQU8VH5dq7T", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136645024002yMnyfYbpQ8Nin5"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "bash", "callID": "call_00_9c2425uk5zcb2dtkz1sgrhxa", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"command": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code && ./gradlew :app:assembleRelease --console=plain 2>&1 | tail -25", "timeout": 2400000}, "output": "(no output)\n\n<shell_metadata>\nUser aborted the command\n</shell_metadata>", "metadata": {"output": "(no output)\n\n<shell_metadata>\nUser aborted the command\n</shell_metadata>", "exit": null, "truncated": false}, "title": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code && ./gradlew :app:assembleRelease --console=plain 2>&1 | tail -25", "time": {"start": 1791913918590, "end": 1791914382065}}, "id": "prt_136647f50001zDETpI09o7Q34b", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136645024002yMnyfYbpQ8Nin5"}]}, {"info": {"role": "user", "time": {"created": 1791914390389}, "agent": "build", "model": {"providerID": "opencode", "modelID": "big-pickle"}, "summary": {"diffs": []}, "id": "msg_1366bb375001ZG54NsMGgXmzoB", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"type": "text", "text": "кмк успехи ", "id": "prt_1366bb380001zrsthl7hNbOhNc", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1366bb375001ZG54NsMGgXmzoB"}]}, {"info": {"parentID": "msg_1366bb375001ZG54NsMGgXmzoB", "role": "assistant", "mode": "build", "agent": "build", "path": {"cwd": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code", "root": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "reasoning": 0, "cache": {"read": 0, "write": 0}}, "modelID": "big-pickle", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1791914394071, "completed": 1791914645125}, "error": {"name": "MessageAbortedError", "data": {"message": "Aborted"}}, "id": "msg_1366bc1d7002zf1iFmu00I6gyl", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_1366bdf7e001QVnDe6iEHQBJ83", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1366bc1d7002zf1iFmu00I6gyl"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "The user aborted the release build and said \"кмк успехи\" = \"IMO/IMHO successes\" (probably \"как мне кажется, успехи\" - seems like progress). They switched from plan to build mode.\n\nSo the user aborted the long release build. They're acknowledging progress. I should summarize what we've achieved and the current state, and maybe not run the 15-min release build again unless needed. But I want to give the actual new release size. Let me reconsider — maybe I can compute more precisely without waiting, or run it in background.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: the user said \"кмк успехи\" — meaning they see progress. Perhaps they want me to wrap up with the summary. But I should still verify the release size if possible. The full release build is long. \n\nLet me think about whether I can get the exact new release size faster. The debug APK build earlier: debug new = 102.2MB compressed (107,767,032 bytes). The old debug would have included classes.dex with dictionary. I don't have old debug. But old release = 87,103,556. The delta = old dict dex (30.16MB) - new asset (11.34MB) = 18.8MB → new release ≈ 68.3MB. Reasonably confident.\n\nLet me at least try to build release again, maybe it was progressing. But user aborted it, likely because it's slow. I shouldn't re-run a 15-min command without need. \n\nLet me instead provide a concise status + summary and ask whether to finish verifying the release APK. Actually, I'm now in build mode and should complete the task. The remaining verification (release APK size) is valuable. But the user aborted... Maybe they aborted due to time. Let me not re-run the full build immediately; instead, summarize progress and confirm the change, and offer to run the release build if they want the exact number.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the whole thing: is the change even correct/desirable? We save ~19MB (87→~68MB). That helps but may not fully fix a device with very little space. I should be honest about that.\n\nAlso, I realize there might be an even better approach that both shrinks more AND keeps speed: store the dictionary in a **compact binary** form that is also smaller in APK and faster to load. But given the user's constraint and time, the current change is reasonable.\n\nLet me finish the remaining tasks:\n1. Run spotless check on changed files (RuWordList.kt, App.kt, gen script). \n2. Mark todos.\n3. Summarize.\n\nLet me run spotless for the data and app modules. `./gradlew :data:spotlessCheck :app:spotlessCheck` — might be slowish but much faster than assemble. Let me run it.\n\nActually spotless for these modules should be quick (formatting check). Let me run.\n\nThen summarize with the numbers.\n\nLet me also double-check: I should not leave the giant 103MB debug APK around? It's in build/ (gitignored). Fine.\n\nLet me run spotlessCheck.", "time": {"start": 1791914401667, "end": 1791914406509}, "id": "prt_1366bdf83001JnfiEQvO0ibfdk", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1366bc1d7002zf1iFmu00I6gyl"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Понял. Подбиваю статус и проверяю форматтер.", "time": {"start": 1791914406513, "end": 1791914407076}, "id": "prt_1366bf271001mA1Aycqt81TFCr", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1366bc1d7002zf1iFmu00I6gyl"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "bash", "callID": "call_00_pwvgfdk7v5evpix86ig49cn4", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"command": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code && ./gradlew :data:spotlessCheck :app:spotlessCheck --console=plain 2>&1 | tail -20", "timeout": 900000}, "output": "(no output)\n\n<shell_metadata>\nUser aborted the command\n</shell_metadata>", "metadata": {"output": "(no output)\n\n<shell_metadata>\nUser aborted the command\n</shell_metadata>", "exit": null, "truncated": false}, "title": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code && ./gradlew :data:spotlessCheck :app:spotlessCheck --console=plain 2>&1 | tail -20", "time": {"start": 1791914407054, "end": 1791914644599}}, "id": "prt_1366bf2f2001xMQCKarzzrJ9qx", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1366bc1d7002zf1iFmu00I6gyl"}]}, {"info": {"role": "user", "time": {"created": 1791914903275}, "agent": "build", "model": {"providerID": "opencode", "modelID": "big-pickle"}, "summary": {"diffs": []}, "id": "msg_1367386eb001wNxvZxrnQQPpjH", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"type": "text", "text": "я заметил в версии 2.0.0 очень медленно прогружается интерфейс а также оцр при первом вызове не предлагает выбрать голоса какими озвучивать а сам пытаеться выбрать что сильно замедляет телефон а также нужно чтобы он использовал тот словарь на 3млн чанками а не целиком а то виснет жестко и не понятно от чего а также когда я вручную выделяю область с текстом и он захватывает рамки либо балуны то в большинстве случаев он не даёт результат вовсе из за ширины либо длины ", "id": "prt_1367386ee0019kHL2Js9ZmVZJu", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1367386eb001wNxvZxrnQQPpjH"}]}, {"info": {"parentID": "msg_1367386eb001wNxvZxrnQQPpjH", "role": "assistant", "mode": "build", "agent": "build", "path": {"cwd": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code", "root": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"total": 136529, "input": 1031, "output": 239, "reasoning": 2267, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 132992}}, "modelID": "big-pickle", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1791914905483, "completed": 1791914933775}, "finish": "tool-calls", "id": "msg_136738f8b002008rtunH1kpU6A", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_13673a8c9001RJBJOLPIJt34O0", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136738f8b002008rtunH1kpU6A"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "The user gave a lot of feedback about v2.0.0 problems:\n\n1. **Интерфейс медленно прогружается** — UI loads slowly.\n2. **OCR при первом вызове не предлагает выбрать \"голоса\" (языки/модели?) какими озвучивать** — On first OCR call, doesn't offer to choose voices/languages, tries to auto-select, which heavily slows the phone.\n3. **Нужно чтобы словарь на 3 млн использовал ЧАНКАМИ, а не целиком** — the 3M dictionary should be loaded in chunks, not entirely, because it hangs hard.\n4. **Ручное выделение области с текстом захватывает рамки/балуны → в большинстве случаев не даёт результат из-за ширины/длины** — when manually selecting a text region, it captures frames/speech bubbles, and mostly returns no result due to width/height constraints.\n\nWait — the user says \"озвучивать\" (voice/tts?) Actually \"голоса какими озвучивать\" — maybe they mean OCR languages/models? Or TTS voices? \"не предлагает выбрать голоса какими озвучивать а сам пытается выбрать что сильно замедляет телефон\" — on first call OCR doesn't offer to choose which language models to use and auto-selects, slowing the phone.\n\nHmm, this is now a broader set of issues. The user wants me to fix these. Since we're in build mode, I should tackle them.\n\nBut this is a LOT. Let me prioritize and be systematic. Let me first understand the current state of code and identify which issues are actionable.\n\nThe most concrete and related to our current change:\n- Issue 3: the 3M dictionary should be loaded in chunks, not entirely (hangs). This directly relates to my RuWordList change. Currently (both old and new) `RuWordList.upper` builds the whole 3M HashSet at once → memory spike and a hang. The user explicitly asks for chunked usage. So I should change the design: instead of building a giant in-memory Set, use the dictionary in a chunked/streaming way, or a more memory-efficient structure.\n\nActually \"использовал тот словарь на 3млн чанками а не целиком\" — use it in chunks, not the whole thing at once. This means the runtime should not hold all 3M in memory / should process incrementally.\n\nHmm, but OcrTextCleaner does membership tests (`word in RuWordList.upper`) for arbitrary words during splitGluedRun. A chunked approach means: maybe store the dictionary sorted on disk and binary-search, or partition by first letter/hash bucket and load only needed buckets lazily.\n\nBut wait — my asset change hasn't even been verified/released. The user is describing v2.0.0 (the old release). They're reporting bugs in v2.0.0 and want them fixed. The dictionary hang is one of them. My change (asset instead of DEX) reduces APK but the runtime still builds the full 3M HashSet → still hangs. So I need to ALSO make it memory-efficient/chunked.\n\nLet me think about a good design:\n- Since only `.upper` membership test is used, we can store the dictionary as a single sorted `String` or a `ByteArray` and binary search without building a HashSet of 3M String objects. That drastically cuts memory (from ~300MB to ~70MB) and avoids the huge allocation/hang. Or use a hash-based approach with a single backing array.\n\nBetter: build an immutable hash structure backed by primitive arrays, loaded from the asset. But that's complex.\n\nSimplest effective: keep the asset text, but instead of splitting into 3M String objects, load the whole file into a single `ByteArray` (71MB) — still big but no per-object overhead. Then membership test = binary search over line offsets, comparing bytes. Memory ~71MB (vs ~300MB) and load = just reading bytes (fast, no 3M object allocations). That would remove the \"hangs hard\" problem substantially.\n\nEven better: store the dictionary sorted, and do binary search on lines. Build a `LongArray` of line start offsets (3M longs = 24MB) + the byte array (71MB) = ~95MB. Or avoid offsets by binary searching directly with newline scanning. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, \"chunks\": partition the dictionary by first character (33 buckets). Load only the bucket needed for a given word on demand, cache it. During `splitGluedRun`, words are tested; typically first letter varies but a single caption uses few first letters. This is genuinely \"chunked\" and keeps memory low. But complexity.\n\nActually, there's a subtlety: the dictionary's purpose is DP segmentation; it tests many substrings. Random access needed. A disk-backed binary search per word would be slow.\n\nGiven the user's priority on not hanging and using chunks, I think the best is:\n- Load the dictionary into a single compact structure lazily, in the background, WITHOUT allocating 3M String objects. Use `ByteArray` + binary search, or a memory-efficient hash set.\n\nHmm, but let me not over-engineer. The user has FOUR issues. Let me address them one at a time, starting with understanding the code.\n\nLet me re-read the user's issues in detail:\n\n1. \"в версии 2.0.0 очень медленно прогружается интерфейс\" — UI loads very slowly. Could be due to app startup doing heavy work (OcrVocabulary.configure, OcrScreenshotBuffer.init on main thread? App.kt line 148). Or the ML Kit OCR initialization. Need to investigate.\n\n2. \"а также оцр при первом вызове не предлагает выбрать голоса какими озвучивать а сам пытается выбрать что сильно замедляет телефон\" — On first OCR invocation, it doesn't prompt to choose which OCR engine/models to use, but auto-selects, which heavily slows the phone. So there should be a first-run prompt to choose OCR engine/models rather than auto-downloading/initializing everything.\n\n3. \"нужно чтобы он использовал тот словарь на 3млн чанками а не целиком а то виснет жестко и не понятно от чего\" — use the 3M dictionary in chunks, not all at once; otherwise it hangs hard and it's unclear why.\n\n4. \"когда я вручную выделяю область с текстом и он захватывает рамки либо балуны то в большинстве случаев он не даёт результат вовсе из за ширины либо длины\" — manual text region selection, when it includes frames/speech bubbles, mostly gives no result due to width/length constraints.\n\nThese are substantial. Given the context (this is a big project, many moving parts), I should probably tackle them incrementally and ask clarifying questions where needed. But the user is clearly frustrated and wants fixes.\n\nGiven the scope, maybe I should prioritize #3 (the dictionary chunking) since it's directly related to what we just did and causes the hang. And #1 (slow UI) and #2 (first OCR prompt) and #4 (manual selection).\n\nThis is a huge amount of work. Let me be strategic: use the todo list, and start by exploring the relevant code. Let me not try to do everything blindly.\n\nLet me first explore:\n- App startup (App.kt) for heavy main-thread work.\n- OCR engine selection / first-run flow.\n- OcrTextCleaner / RuWordList usage (dictionary).\n- Manual region selection OCR path (crop/size constraints).\n\nGiven the user's feedback is about v2.0.0 behavior, and we're in build mode, let me investigate each. Let me spawn explore agents in parallel for efficiency.\n\nActually, let me be careful about scope and time. The user might want all four. Let me start by acknowledging and creating a plan/todos, then investigate. Let me use the explore agent to gather info on all four areas in parallel.\n\nLet me launch parallel exploration tasks.\n\nBut first, let me note: the current working tree has my dictionary→asset changes uncommitted, and the release build was aborted. The user's issues are about v2.0.0 (old). But they want the dictionary chunked — which supersedes my current HashSet approach. I'll need to rework RuWordList to be memory-efficient/chunked.\n\nLet me explore the codebase for:\n1. Startup main-thread work & slow UI.\n2. First-run OCR engine/model selection flow.\n3. OCR manual region selection + size constraints.\n4. (Already know RuWordList.)\n\nLet me dispatch explore agents.\n\nActually, let me first ask the user to prioritize/confirm, because doing all four is a lot and may take many iterations. But the user just gave a clear list; they want them fixed. Given \"IMPORTANT: keep responses short\", I'll create todos and start investigating. I think it's better to investigate first, then implement the most tractable fixes.\n\nHmm, but I should be mindful: this could balloon. Let me ask a focused question on priority? The user listed 4 issues. I think I should:\n1. Investigate all four.\n2. Fix the dictionary chunking (clear, related).\n3. Propose fixes for the others.\n\nLet me start exploring. Launch 3-4 explore tasks in parallel.\n\nLet me define thorough exploration prompts.\n\nTask A: Startup / UI slow. Find what runs on main thread at app startup (App.kt, MainActivity, Application.onCreate), OCR model init, database migrations, etc. Return file:line of heavy synchronous work.\n\nTask B: OCR first-run engine/model selection. Find how OCR engine is chosen, whether there's a first-run dialog, and what gets auto-initialized/downloaded (ML Kit, Tesseract, etc.). Return relevant files/functions.\n\nTask C: Manual region OCR selection. Find the code path for manual crop/region selection, and any width/length/aspect constraints that would reject results. Return file:line of constraints.\n\nTask D: Dictionary usage (OcrTextCleaner.splitGluedRun, RuWordList). I mostly know this, but let me get details of how `upper` is consumed to design chunked loading.\n\nLet me launch A, B, C in parallel (D I can do myself while waiting? No, tool calls are one message; I can include D too).\n\nLet me launch 4 explore tasks.\n\nNote: the explore agent has read tools. Good.\n\nLet me write detailed prompts.", "time": {"start": 1791914912026, "end": 1791914930713}, "id": "prt_13673a91a001fcrgNf6ayMuQ1b", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136738f8b002008rtunH1kpU6A"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Понял — это отдельный список проблем v2.0.0. Разберу по частям. Сначала соберу факты по всем четырём, параллельно.", "time": {"start": 1791914930736, "end": 1791914932342}, "id": "prt_13673f230001P8UkyKvrdDD6gd", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136738f8b002008rtunH1kpU6A"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "todowrite", "callID": "call_00_68n74i7rp18dvodn6j0ng2ka", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"todos": [{"content": "Диагностика: медленный старт UI v2.0.0", "priority": "high", "status": "in_progress"}, {"content": "Диагностика: OCR первый вызов — нет выбора моделей/языков, автоinit тормозит", "priority": "high", "status": "pending"}, {"content": "Словарь 3млн: загрузка чанками/без зависания (переделать RuWordList)", "priority": "high", "status": "pending"}, {"content": "Ручное выделение области: не даёт результат из-за ширины/длины", "priority": "high", "status": "pending"}]}, "output": "[\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Диагностика: медленный старт UI v2.0.0\",\n    \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Диагностика: OCR первый вызов — нет выбора моделей/языков, автоinit тормозит\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Словарь 3млн: загрузка чанками/без зависания (переделать RuWordList)\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Ручное выделение области: не даёт результат из-за ширины/длины\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  }\n]", "metadata": {"todos": [{"content": "Диагностика: медленный старт UI v2.0.0", "status": "in_progress", "priority": "high"}, {"content": "Диагностика: OCR первый вызов — нет выбора моделей/языков, автоinit тормозит", "status": "pending", "priority": "high"}, {"content": "Словарь 3млн: загрузка чанками/без зависания (переделать RuWordList)", "status": "pending", "priority": "high"}, {"content": "Ручное выделение области: не даёт результат из-за ширины/длины", "status": "pending", "priority": "high"}], "truncated": false}, "title": "4 todos", "time": {"start": 1791914932304, "end": 1791914932324}}, "id": "prt_13673f319001UaqopA9Qv3YfLq", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136738f8b002008rtunH1kpU6A"}, {"reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-finish", "tokens": {"total": 136529, "input": 1031, "output": 239, "reasoning": 2267, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 132992}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_13673fb48001SkCoKLGd9tiLZB", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136738f8b002008rtunH1kpU6A"}]}, {"info": {"parentID": "msg_1367386eb001wNxvZxrnQQPpjH", "role": "assistant", "mode": "build", "agent": "build", "path": {"cwd": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code", "root": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "reasoning": 0, "cache": {"read": 0, "write": 0}}, "modelID": "big-pickle", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1791914935908, "completed": 1791915934331}, "error": {"name": "MessageAbortedError", "data": {"message": "Aborted"}}, "id": "msg_136740664002noSSiqmqT8lo2U", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_1367418f1001ihq4nObl0lE9Ds", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136740664002noSSiqmqT8lo2U"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "Let me launch parallel exploration tasks for the four areas. I'll use the explore agent.\n\nActually, let me be judicious about how many agents. I'll launch 3 explore tasks (UI startup, OCR first-run engine selection, manual region selection) and handle the dictionary myself since I know it. Let me include the dictionary consumer investigation too.\n\nLet me write the prompts.", "time": {"start": 1791914940782, "end": 1791914941175}, "id": "prt_13674196e001cgUKWZJ10lRM0z", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136740664002noSSiqmqT8lo2U"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "task", "callID": "call_00_scvknc8pt1wgyby6bxtsb3px", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"description": "Explore app startup slowness", "prompt": "Repo: /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code — an Android app \"Yomikai\" (manga reader with OCR). Kotlin, multi-module Gradle.\n\nGOAL: Find the causes of slow app startup / slow UI loading in version 2.0.0. This is research only — do NOT modify any files.\n\nInvestigate and report with exact file:line references:\n1. Everything that runs on the main/UI thread during application startup: `Application.onCreate` (app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/App.kt), `MainActivity` onCreate/init, any `Injekt`/DI module initialization, database/SQLDelight setup, migration scripts, preference loads.\n2. Any heavy synchronous work done on the main thread at startup (file I/O, database open, building large in-memory structures, OCR model init, dictionary loading).\n3. OCR-related init that happens automatically at startup or first launch (search for OcrScanManager, OcrScreenshotBuffer, ensureOcrModelsInstalled, OcrModelDownloader, ML Kit / Tesseract / LiteRT initialization).\n4. Whether any of the above is dispatched to background threads and how (Thread {}, coroutines, WorkManager).\n5. Any obvious main-thread I/O or `runBlocking` on startup.\n\nSearch hints: grep for \"onCreate\", \"runBlocking\", \"init(\", \"OcrS\", \"Injekt.importModule\", \"Thread {\", \"Dispatchers.Main\", \"ensureOcr\", \"SQLite\", \"migrat\".\n\nReturn a concise ranked list (most likely culprits first) of file:line + what it does + whether it's on main thread.", "subagent_type": "explore"}, "output": "<task id=\"ses_ec98bd937ffeRLPJkwArMMCjIQ\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nDownloader constructor uses launchNow { store.restore() } — background (launchNow likely Dispatchers.IO? Let me not verify). The eager gets: sourceManager, chapterCache, downloadPreferences, ocrPreferences, xml, getCategories, getTracks are resolved via Injekt.get() at construction. get<GetCategories>() is an addFactory (new GetCategories(get())) — triggers get<CategoryRepository>() → CategoryRepositoryImpl(get()) → get<Database>(). Already constructed. get<GetTracks>() similarly. chapterCache already constructed. So DownloadManager construction on main resolves several interactors + Downloader + DownloadStore(context) constructor (light). DownloadStore's restore is in launchNow. So moderately heavy but mostly DB object refs.\n\nOK, enough. Let me now write the report.\n\nActually, one more important thing: Is AppModule's getMainExecutor block invoked during App.onCreate? `Injekt.importModule(AppModule(this))` at App.kt:131 calls registerInjectables, which calls ContextCompat.getMainExecutor(app).execute { ... }. Since we're on main, this posts a Runnable to the main Looper queue; it runs after the current message (App.onCreate) finishes but before/around Activity onCreate? Actually Activity launch and Application.onCreate are in the same message? Application.onCreate is called during ActivityThread.handleBindApplication, before the Activity is created, all on main. The posted runnable will run after handleBindApplication completes, likely before or interleaved with the launch Activity's onCreate messages. Either way, on main during startup.\n\nLet me finalize. I'll include exact file:line.\n\nLet me get precise line numbers for key references:\n- App.kt:90 onCreate; 130-132 importModule; 138 Thread OcrScanManager; 146-150 OcrVocabulary; 156 RuWordList; 160 OcrScreenshotBuffer.init; 162 maxEntries; 228-230 hardwareBitmap; 236 themeMode; 251 initializeMigrator; 255-268; 364-384 ensureOcrModelsInstalled.\n- MainActivity.kt:156 onCreate; 177 ensureOcrModelsInstalled; 179 awaitAndRelease; 190 getIncognitoState.await; 300-303 splash.\n- Migrator.kt:13 scope IO; 15-27 initialize; 38-40 runBlocking.\n- MigrationJobFactory.kt:22 async UNDISPATCHED.\n- AppModule.kt:71-85 SqlDriver; 86-101 Database; 134 AndroidSourceManager; 135 ExtensionManager; 151-160 getMainExecutor.\n- ExtensionManager.kt:74-77 init; 120-132 initExtensions.\n- ExtensionLoader.kt:120-171 loadExtensions (124 getInstalledPackages; 166-171 runBlocking).\n- OcrScreenshotBuffer.kt:91-99 init; 482-495 load; 460-480 persist.\n- OcrVocabulary.kt:43-63 configure.\n- RuWordList.kt:65-67 configure; 79-97 upper lazy.\n- WidgetManager.kt:22-41.\n- SetupBackupCreateMigration.kt:11-15; BackupCreateJob.kt:90-114.\n- SetupLibraryUpdateMigration.kt:11-15; LibraryUpdateJob.kt:413-459.\n- TrustExtensionRepositoryMigration.kt:14-28.\n- CategoryPreferencesCleanupMigration.kt:13-38.\n- WorkManager default init: no Configuration.Provider; manifest provider ShizukuProvider:321.\n\nLet me write it up concisely and ranked.</think>I have gathered enough evidence. Here is the ranked report.\n\n# Yomikai 2.0.0 startup slowness — findings (research only)\n\n## Summary of the critical structural problem\nTwo large, independent main-thread blocks exist before the first frame is drawn:\n1. `MainActivity.onCreate` literally **`runBlocking`s on the UI thread** waiting for all DB/WorkManager migrations (`MainActivity.kt:179`).\n2. `AppModule` claims to init expensive singletons \"asynchronously\" but uses `ContextCompat.getMainExecutor(...)` — i.e. the **main thread** (`AppModule.kt:151-160`). This constructs the SQLite `Database`, OkHttp `NetworkHelper`, `SourceManager` → `ExtensionManager` (which synchronously loads every extension APK), and `DownloadManager` on the UI thread.\n\nAdditionally, two OCR stores are read from disk synchronously during `Application.onCreate` (`App.kt:148`, `App.kt:160`).\n\n---\n\n## Ranked culprits\n\n### 1. `Migrator.awaitAndRelease()` — runBlocking on the main thread\n- `app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/ui/main/MainActivity.kt:179` calls `Migrator.awaitAndRelease()` directly in `onCreate` (main thread).\n- `app/src/main/java/mihon/core/migration/Migrator.kt:38-40` implements it as `runBlocking { await()... }`.\n- Effect: the UI thread is **fully blocked until every registered migration finishes** (DB queries, WorkManager enqueue, preferences). Because the splash `ready` flag is only set later in a `LaunchedEffect` (`MainActivity.kt:215-230`, splash kept up to `SPLASH_MAX_DURATION=5000`, line 556), this directly shows up as a slow/long splash.\n- Migrations are started from `App.kt:251` → `initializeMigrator()` (`App.kt:255-268`).\n- Worse: `app/src/main/java/mihon/core/migration/MigrationJobFactory.kt:22` uses `async(start = CoroutineStart.UNDISPATCHED)`, so the **first non-suspending migrations execute on the caller's thread (main)** during `App.onCreate`. The `ALWAYS` ones sort first (`Migration.ALWAYS = -1f`, `Migration.kt:12`):\n  - `SetupBackupCreateMigration.kt:11-15` → `BackupCreateJob.setupTask` → `context.workManager.enqueueUniquePeriodicWork(...)` (blocking WorkManager DB/disk write) — `BackupCreateJob.kt:90-114`, no `withIOContext`.\n  - `SetupLibraryUpdateMigration.kt:11-15` → `LibraryUpdateJob.setupTask` → same `enqueueUniquePeriodicWork` — `LibraryUpdateJob.kt:413-459`.\n  - `InstallationIdMigration.kt:13-17` preference read/write, no `withIOContext`.\n- Upgrade path additionally blocks on IO migrations: `TrustExtensionRepositoryMigration.kt:14`, `CategoryPreferencesCleanupMigration.kt:13`, `SetupDictionaryOcrPresentationMigration.kt:13`, `VerticalNavigatorMigration.kt:13`.\n- Verdict: **on main thread** (runBlocking) and the first `ALWAYS` migrations also execute on main. Highest-impact.\n\n### 2. `AppModule` \"async\" init is actually the main thread\n`app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/di/AppModule.kt:151-160`\n```\n// Asynchronously init expensive components for a faster cold start\nContextCompat.getMainExecutor(app).execute {\n    get<NetworkHelper>(); get<SourceManager>(); get<Database>(); get<DownloadManager>()\n}\n```\n`getMainExecutor` = main thread. Each of these is heavy:\n- `get<Database>()` (`AppModule.kt:86-101`) resolves the `SqlDriver` (`AppModule.kt:71-85`: `BundledSQLiteDriver` + `AndroidxSqliteDriver(... schema = Database.Schema ...)`), i.e. **opens `tachiyomi.db` and runs schema create/migration on the UI thread**.\n- `get<SourceManager>()` (`AppModule.kt:134`) constructs `AndroidSourceManager` (`AndroidSourceManager.kt:27`), which requires `ExtensionManager` (`AppModule.kt:135`). `ExtensionManager`'s `init` (`ExtensionManager.kt:74-77`) calls `initExtensions()` (`ExtensionManager.kt:120-132`), which calls `ExtensionLoader.loadExtensions` (`ExtensionLoader.kt:120-171`): `PackageManager.getInstalledPackages(...)` (line 124) plus **`runBlocking { extPkgs.map { async { loadExtension } }.awaitAll() }`** (lines 166-171) — loading every installed extension APK/class on the main thread. This is likely the single largest UI-thread stall.\n- `get<NetworkHelper>()` (`AppModule.kt:131`) → `NetworkHelper.kt:18-92` builds OkHttp clients, 5 MB disk cache, cookie jar, DoH, proxy/interceptor setup.\n- `get<DownloadManager>()` (`AppModule.kt:138`) → `DownloadManager.kt:36-56` constructs `Downloader` (`Downloader.kt:75-125`, resolves several DB interactors + `DownloadStore`), `DownloadPendingDeleter`.\n- Verdict: **on main thread** despite the comment.\n\n### 3. `OcrScreenshotBuffer.init()` — synchronous JSON read at `Application.onCreate`\n- `app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/App.kt:160` calls `mihon.data.ocr.OcrScreenshotBuffer.init(applicationContext)` directly in `onCreate`.\n- `data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/OcrScreenshotBuffer.kt:91-99` → `load()` at `OcrScreenshotBuffer.kt:482-495` does `file.readText()` + `json.decodeFromString<List<OcrScreenshotEntry>>` synchronously, for up to `maxEntries` (default 50, line 43) entries each containing OCR regions.\n- Verdict: **on main thread** file I/O + JSON parse. Clear culprit.\n\n### 4. `OcrVocabulary.configure()` — synchronous user-dictionary file read at startup\n- `app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/App.kt:148-150` calls `mihon.data.ocr.OcrVocabulary.configure(path)` in `onCreate`.\n- `data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/OcrVocabulary.kt:43-63`: `active.useLines { ... }` reads and tokenizes the entire `ocr_vocab.txt` (grows over time as words are learned), synchronously.\n- Verdict: **on main thread**; size depends on accumulated user words.\n\n### 5. `GetIncognitoState.await(null)` during first composition\n- `app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/ui/main/MainActivity.kt:190`: `remember { mutableStateOf(getIncognitoState.await(null)) }` runs during composition (main). `GetIncognitoState.kt:15-21` reads `BasePreferences.incognitoMode`; constructing it injects `ExtensionManager` (`GetIncognitoState.kt:10-14`), which may trigger #2's extension loading if not already done.\n- Verdict: **on main thread**; mainly a pref read but linked to extension-manager construction.\n\n### 6. `WidgetManager.init` → widget `updateAll` on main\n- `app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/App.kt:239` wires `WidgetManager(...).init(scope)`.\n- `presentation-widget/.../WidgetManager.kt:22-41`: `getUpdates.subscribe(...)` / prefs are `.flowOn(Dispatchers.Default)`, but the downstream `.onEach { UpdatesGridGlanceWidget().updateAll(this); ... }` (lines 32-39) runs on the `launchIn(scope)` context, i.e. the ProcessLifecycle **main** scope. `updateAll` does Glance widget work (queries/IO).\n- Verdict: partially main (the `onEach`/`updateAll` part); triggers on first flow emission at startup.\n\n### 7. Miscellaneous main-thread preference reads/writes during `App.onCreate`\n- `App.kt:162` `Injekt.get<OcrPreferences>().screenshotBufferSize().get()`.\n- `App.kt:228-230` `hardwareBitmapThreshold.isSet()/set(...)` (write).\n- `App.kt:236` `setAppCompatDelegateThemeMode(Injekt.get<UiPreferences>().themeMode.get())`.\n- `App.kt:256-258` `last_version_code` read used to decide migrations.\n- `MainActivity.kt:191` `preferences.downloadedOnly.collectAsState()` and `192` `downloadCache.isInitializing` (DownloadCache is mostly background; `DownloadCache.kt:102-124` uses IO scope).\n- Verdict: each individually small, but they add up on the UI thread.\n\n### 8. Injekt module registration\n- `app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/App.kt:130-132` `Injekt.importModule(PreferenceModule/AppModule/DomainModule)` runs on main. Registration itself is cheap (lambdas), but it is where the AppModule main-executor runnable (#2) is posted, and DomainModule factories get resolved eagerly by #2.\n\n---\n\n## Items that are correctly off the main thread (not culprits)\n- `App.kt:97` Telemetry/Firebase init → `Thread` (MIN_PRIORITY).\n- `App.kt:105-117` `AiHttpServer.start` → `Thread`.\n- `App.kt:138-140` `Injekt.get<OcrScanManager>().startIfPending()` → `Thread` (`OcrScanManager.kt:45-49`).\n- `App.kt:168-183` first-run directory creation → `Thread`.\n- `App.kt:364-384` `ensureOcrModelsInstalled()` → `Thread` (MIN_PRIORITY); called from `MainActivity.kt:177`. Correctly background (downloads ~21 MB).\n- `Migrator.scope = Dispatchers.IO` (`Migrator.kt:13`), `OcrModelDownloader.scope` IO (`OcrModelDownloader.kt:228`), `OcrRepositoryImpl.scope` IO (`OcrRepositoryImpl.kt:179`), `AndroidSourceManager.scope` IO (`AndroidSourceManager.kt:38`), `DownloadCache.scope` IO (`DownloadCache.kt:72`).\n\n## First-use (not startup, but relevant to \"slow UI loading\")\n- `data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/RuWordList.kt:79-97`: the `upper` lazy allocates a `HashSet` for up to `EXPECTED_FORMS = 3_014_492` forms and reads the asset on first OCR text-clean (`OcrTextCleaner.kt:468`). `App.kt:156` only sets the opener, so this is deferred, but the first OCR pass pays a large CPU/memory cost.\n\n## Systemic (not Yomikai-specific code, but main-thread at process start)\n- No `androidx.work.Configuration.Provider` exists in code, so WorkManager initializes through `androidx.startup.InitializationProvider` (merged manifest) on the main thread at process start.\n- `app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml:321-327` `rikka.shizuku.ShizukuProvider` `onCreate` also runs on the main thread when the process starts.\n\n---\n\n## Bottom line (most → least likely)\n1. `Migrator.awaitAndRelease()` `runBlocking` on main — `MainActivity.kt:179` (+ `async(UNDISPATCHED)` migrations on main — `MigrationJobFactory.kt:22`).\n2. `AppModule.kt:151-160` `getMainExecutor` building `Database` / `NetworkHelper` / `ExtensionManager` (loads all extensions via `runBlocking`, `ExtensionLoader.kt:166`) / `DownloadManager` on main.\n3. `OcrScreenshotBuffer.init` synchronous JSON read — `App.kt:160` → `OcrScreenshotBuffer.kt:482-495`.\n4. `OcrVocabulary.configure` synchronous file read — `App.kt:148` → `OcrVocabulary.kt:43-63`.\n5. `getIncognitoState.await(null)` in composition — `MainActivity.kt:190`.\n6. `WidgetManager` `updateAll` on main — `App.kt:239` → `WidgetManager.kt:32-39`.\n7. Assorted pref I/O in `App.kt:162,228-230,236,256-258`.\n8. Deferred `RuWordList.upper` (~3 M forms) on first OCR — `RuWordList.kt:79-97`.\n</task_result>\n</task>", "metadata": {"parentSessionId": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "sessionId": "ses_ec98bd937ffeRLPJkwArMMCjIQ", "model": {"modelID": "big-pickle", "providerID": "opencode"}, "truncated": false}, "title": "Explore app startup slowness", "time": {"start": 1791914944223, "end": 1791915213026}}, "id": "prt_136741afe001u2W7Eyl0TJWzO0", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136740664002noSSiqmqT8lo2U"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "task", "callID": "call_01_9zb8uvjjbfxxl84o26qrmlgg", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"description": "Explore OCR engine selection flow", "prompt": "Repo: /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code — Android app \"Yomikai\" (manga reader with built-in OCR). Kotlin.\n\nGOAL: Understand the OCR engine / language-model selection flow, and why the first OCR invocation auto-selects an engine/model instead of letting the user choose, causing the phone to slow down. Research only — do NOT modify files.\n\nInvestigate and report with exact file:line references:\n1. Where OCR engines are defined and selected: search for OcrEngine, OcrPlugins, CyrillicOcrEngine, MlKitOcrEngine, TesseractOcrEngine, GoogleAiOcrEngine, OpenRouterOcrEngine, FastOcrEngine, GlensOcrEngine, LegacyOcrEngine, OwOcrEngine.\n2. How the \"active/default\" OCR engine is chosen on first use. Is there any first-run prompt/dialog letting the user pick an engine or language model? (search for settings screens: ui/setting, OcrPreferences, pref keys like ocr.*). \n3. What happens automatically on first OCR run: which models are downloaded or initialized eagerly, and whether multiple engines get initialized at once (which would slow the device).\n4. The OCR language / script selection (\"voices\"/languages): where languages are enumerated and chosen, and whether there's a chooser UI.\n5. Any place that initializes ALL engines or ALL models eagerly vs lazily.\n\nSearch hints: grep for \"OcrEngine\", \"activeEngine\", \"selectedEngine\", \"isInstalled\", \"download\", \"OcrPreferences\", \"pref_ocr\", \"engine\", \"language\", \"script\".\n\nReturn: a concise map of the selection flow (entry point -> default pick -> init/download), with file:line references, and call out exactly where a first-run chooser is missing and where eager init happens.", "subagent_type": "explore"}, "output": "<task id=\"ses_ec98bcc83ffeL9j6T0sVS3UR8y\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI now have a complete picture. Here is the investigation report.\n\n---\n\n# OCR engine / model selection flow — Yomikai\n\n## 1. Where OCR engines are defined and selected\n\n**Engine interface and implementations**\n- `OcrEngine` interface — `data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/OcrEngine.kt:9`; `LineOcrEngine` — `OcrEngine.kt:29`\n- `CyrillicOcrEngine` — `data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/CyrillicOcrEngine.kt:38` (local PP-OCRv3+v5)\n- `MlKitOcrEngine` — `data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/MlKitOcrEngine.kt:27`\n- `TesseractOcrEngine` — `data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/TesseractOcrEngine.kt:35`\n- `GoogleAiOcrEngine` — `.../GoogleAiOcrEngine.kt:21`\n- `OpenRouterOcrEngine` — `.../OpenRouterOcrEngine.kt:20`\n- `FastOcrEngine` — `.../FastOcrEngine.kt:26`\n- `GlensOcrEngine` — `.../GlensOcrEngine.kt:22`\n- `LegacyOcrEngine` — `.../LegacyOcrEngine.kt:23`\n- `OwOcrEngine` — `.../OwOcrEngine.kt:67`\n- `ZenFreeOcrEngine` — `.../ZenFreeOcrEngine.kt:18`\n- Detector wrapper `CyrillicDetOcrEngine` / `UnavailableDetOcrEngine` — `.../DetOcrEngine.kt:13,30`\n\n**Declarative registry** — `data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/OcrPlugins.kt:67`\n- Descriptors: `CYRILLIC` `:69`, `TESSERACT` `:88`, `MLKIT` `:103`, `GLENS` `:116`, `ZEN_FREE` `:127`, `GOOGLE_AI` `:139`, `OPENROUTER` `:150`, `OWOCR` `:161`; ordered list `ALL` `:179`.\n- Legacy aliasing (`LEGACY`/`FAST` → Cyrillic) — `:173-176`, `byModel()` `:195-196`.\n\n**Instance factory / selection** — `data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/OcrRepositoryImpl.kt`\n- Engine fields (caches) — `:110-123`\n- `EngineType` enum — `:210-222`\n- `selectedEngineType()` — `:224`; `engineTypeOf()` — `:233-253`\n- `engineFor(type)` lazily creates one engine — `:360-417`\n- `offlineEngines` / `onlineEngines` fallback pools — `:274-292`\n- `fallbackChain()` — `:327-348`\n\n## 2. Active/default engine choice on first use\n\n- The persisted preference is `pref_ocr_model`, **defaulting to `OcrModel.CYRILLIC`**:\n  - `OcrRepositoryImpl.kt:40` → `preferenceStore.getEnum(\"pref_ocr_model\", OcrModel.CYRILLIC)`\n  - `domain/.../OcrPreferences.kt:17` → same default\n- `recognizeText()` resolves the engine with no user input: `OcrRepositoryImpl.kt:584` (`model?.let(::engineTypeOf) ?: selectedEngineType()`); `scanPage()` at `:677`; `askAboutImage()` at `:623`.\n- **There is no first-run engine/model chooser dialog.** The only onboarding touchpoint is `OcrModelStep` (`app/.../onboarding/OcrModelStep.kt:33`), and it is *not* an engine chooser:\n  - `isComplete = true` (`:35`) — never blocks, skippable.\n  - It offers only \"Download Cyrillic OCR\" vs \"Download later\" (`:65-127`); clicking card 0 forcibly sets `OcrModel.CYRILLIC` (`:68`) and starts the download (`:69`). The model was already the default anyway.\n  - It is registered in the onboarding list at `OnboardingScreen.kt:42`.\n- Real choosers (all post-hoc, buried in settings/reader):\n  - `SettingsHubScreen.kt` OCR tab \"Движок распознавания\" — `:882-911`\n  - `SettingsOcrScreen.getEnginesGroup` — `SettingsOcrScreen.kt:349-359`\n  - Reader quick switcher `OcrModelQuickSwitcher` — `ReaderTopBar.kt:151-255`\n  - `LocalOcrScreens.EngineOptions` — `LocalOcrScreens.kt:166-188`\n  - `SettingsOcrPluginsScreen.kt` is **read-only** (\"Экран ничего не переключает\", `:24`).\n\n## 3. What happens automatically on first OCR run (eager work)\n\nTwo eager paths run **without any user choice**:\n\n**(a) App startup auto-download** — `MainActivity.onCreate()` calls `ensureOcrModelsInstalled()` at `app/.../ui/main/MainActivity.kt:177`, defined at `app/.../App.kt:364-384`:\n- Unconditionally migrates `LEGACY`/`FAST`/`TESSERACT` → `CYRILLIC` (`App.kt:368-377`).\n- If `cyrillic_ocr` is not installed, starts `downloadPack(..., \"cyrillic_ocr\")` (`App.kt:379-380`) on a `Thread.MIN_PRIORITY` named `cyrillic-ocr-init` (`:383`).\n- Pack is ~21 MB / 5 files — `OcrModelDownloader.kt:125-131` (detector, v3, v5, 2 dicts), URLs `:172-174`, mirrors `:202-213`.\n- Startup also resumes queued scans: `App.kt:138` → `OcrScanManager.startIfPending()` (`OcrScanManager.kt:45`).\n\n**(b) Reader open warms up the engine eagerly** — `ReaderActivity.onCreate()` calls `viewModel.warmupOcr()` at `ui/reader/ReaderActivity.kt:545`, defined at `ReaderViewModel.kt:900-913`:\n- It builds a 64×64 bitmap and calls `ocrProcessor.getText(...)` (`:907`) → `OcrProcessor.getText` → `OcrRepository.recognizeText` (`OcrProcessor.kt:10-12`) → default `CYRILLIC` engine.\n- That constructs `CyrillicOcrEngine` (`OcrRepositoryImpl.kt:363-368`) and calls `ensureInitialized()` → `init()` (`CyrillicOcrEngine.kt:156-209`), which loads **three TFLite models** (detector + v3 + v5) and **two dictionaries** (`:175-191`) using `availableProcessors().coerceIn(2,4)` CPU threads (`:171-174`). This is the main CPU/RAM spike and the \"phone slows down\" symptom.\n\nNo multiple engines are initialized at once in the normal path: `engineFor` instantiates lazily one engine at a time and caches (`OcrRepositoryImpl.kt:360-417`). The eager cost is the 21 MB `cyrillic_ocr` download plus the 3-model/2-thread Cyrillic init, both triggered before the user ever picks an engine.\n\nOther implicit downloads (on demand, not first-run): Tesseract data auto-downloaded when Tesseract is selected — `SettingsHubScreen.kt:891-908` → `OcrModelDownloader.ensureTesseractData` (`OcrModelDownloader.kt:284-299`); panel detector `ensurePanelDetector` (`:263-272`, now unused per `DomainModule.kt:323`).\n\n## 4. Language / script selection (\"voices\"/languages)\n\n- Auto-read language `pref_autoread_language`, **default `\"ru\"`** — `OcrPreferences.kt:242`.\n  - Chooser in settings hub — `SettingsHubScreen.kt:642-645, 708-720` (ru/en/ja/ko/zh/any).\n  - In-reader chooser — `OcrBubbleSettingsDialog.kt:67, 190`.\n- This language drives engine remapping: `readsCyrillic()` (`OcrRepositoryImpl.kt:256`) + `isCyrillicOcrLanguage()` (`OcrPlugins.kt:271-274`); because the default is `\"ru\"`, `engineTypeOf()` silently rewrites `MLKIT` → `CYRILLIC` (`OcrRepositoryImpl.kt:249-252`).\n- Per-engine language settings:\n  - Glens language/region — `OcrPreferences.kt:107-108`; chooser `SettingsOcrScreen.kt:384-429`.\n  - Tesseract langs `pref_tess_langs` default `\"eng+rus\"` — `OcrPreferences.kt:311`; chooser `SettingsHubScreen.kt:1132, 1172`.\n- No language/script prompt fires before the first OCR; it uses the `\"ru\"` default. (Voice/TTS enumeration is separate — `OcrPreferences.kt:130-206`, `TtsVoicePickerDialog.kt`.)\n\n## 5. Eager vs lazy initialization summary\n\n- **Lazy:** engines are created on demand in `engineFor` and cached (`OcrRepositoryImpl.kt:360-417`); only the primary engine (plus on-failure fallbacks) is touched (`recognizeWithFallback` `:466-514`, `scanPageWithFallback` `:776-833`). `closeEngines()` tears all down — `:1338-1377`.\n- **Eager:**\n  1. `cyrillic_ocr` (~21 MB) auto-download at every app start — `App.kt:364-384`, `MainActivity.kt:177`; files `OcrModelDownloader.kt:125-131`.\n  2. Cyrillic model init (3 TFLite + 2 dicts, 2–4 threads) on every reader open — `ReaderViewModel.kt:900-913`, `ReaderActivity.kt:545`, `CyrillicOcrEngine.kt:163-209`.\n  3. Pending scan queue resumed at startup — `App.kt:138`.\n  4. `OcrPluginAvailability.availableIds()` creates+closes a LiteRT environment on every settings/hub composition — `OcrPluginAvailability.kt:28-30`, called from `SettingsOcrPluginsScreen.kt:40-52` and `SettingsOcrScreen.kt:77-90`.\n\n---\n\n## Selection flow map\n\n```\nEngine registry            OcrPlugins.ALL                       OcrPlugins.kt:179\n        │                  descriptors :69-170\n        ▼\nDefault pref (no prompt)   pref_ocr_model = CYRILLIC           OcrRepositoryImpl.kt:40\n                                                               OcrPreferences.kt:17\n        ▼\nResolver                   selectedEngineType() :224           OcrRepositoryImpl.kt:224\n                           engineTypeOf() :233-253 (MLKIT→CYRILLIC if ru :252)\n        ▼\nEager on app start         ensureOcrModelsInstalled()          App.kt:364-384\n                           ← MainActivity.kt:177\n                           auto-downloads cyrillic_ocr 21MB    OcrModelDownloader.kt:125-131\n        ▼\nEager on reader open       warmupOcr()                        ReaderViewModel.kt:900\n                           ← ReaderActivity.kt:545\n                           → CyrillicOcrEngine.init()           CyrillicOcrEngine.kt:163\n                             loads det+v3+v5+2 dicts, 2-4 thr  CyrillicOcrEngine.kt:171-191\n        ▼\nLazy per-request           engineFor(type) one cached engine  OcrRepositoryImpl.kt:360\n        ▼\nUser choosers (post-hoc)   SettingsHubScreen.kt:882            (only after the fact)\n                           SettingsOcrScreen.kt:349\n                           ReaderTopBar.kt:151\n```\n\n## Called-out gaps\n\n- **Missing first-run chooser:** there is no prompt letting the user pick an engine/model before first use. The engine is silently defaulted to `CYRILLIC` at `OcrRepositoryImpl.kt:40` / `OcrPreferences.kt:17`. The onboarding `OcrModelStep` (`OcrModelStep.kt:33`) is only a download-now/later card, is always \"complete\" (`:35`), and hard-sets `CYRILLIC` (`:68`).\n- **Eager init/download sites:** `App.kt:364-384` (startup 21 MB download, called from `MainActivity.kt:177`) and `ReaderViewModel.kt:900` (reader-open model warm-up, called from `ReaderActivity.kt:545`), which together load/download the Cyrillic pack and the 3 large TFLite models + dictionaries (`CyrillicOcrEngine.kt:163-209`) before the user has made any selection — the likely cause of the perceived slowdown.\n</task_result>\n</task>", "metadata": {"parentSessionId": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "sessionId": "ses_ec98bcc83ffeL9j6T0sVS3UR8y", "model": {"modelID": "big-pickle", "providerID": "opencode"}, "truncated": false}, "title": "Explore OCR engine selection flow", "time": {"start": 1791914947462, "end": 1791915102955}}, "id": "prt_136742701001st6QI9TbS8DZ5S", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136740664002noSSiqmqT8lo2U"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "task", "callID": "call_02_5e1jb67tz1g4jeuvqxxsiwf1", "state": {"status": "error", "input": {"description": "Explore manual region OCR selection", "prompt": "Repo: /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code — Android app \"Yomikai\" (manga reader with built-in OCR). Kotlin.\n\nGOAL: Understand the manual text-region selection OCR path, and why selecting a region that includes frames/speech-bubble borders (рамки, балуны) mostly returns no result due to width/length constraints. Research only — do NOT modify files.\n\nInvestigate and report with exact file:line references:\n1. The code path for manually selecting a rectangular region on screen and running OCR on it (search for \"selection\", \"crop\", \"region\", \"overlay\", \"OcrOverlay\", \"gesture\", \"manual\", \"rect\", \"Bounds\", \"RectF\").\n2. All validation / acceptance filters applied to the OCR result that could reject it based on aspect ratio, width, height, minimum/maximum size, or text length. Search for thresholds like \"minWidth\", \"minHeight\", \"aspect\", \"coerceIn\", \"width\", \"height\", \"MIN_\", \"MAX_\", \"isAcceptable\", \"acceptableAfterSalvage\", \"looksLike\", \"fragment\", \"coverage\".\n3. Specifically: OcrTextCleaner (data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/OcrTextCleaner.kt), CyrillicOcrEngine, OcrRegionRules, OcrBoxGeometry, and any acceptance heuristics in the app module under ui/reader or ui/ocr.\n4. Any place a crop is expanded/shrunk to content, or where an image that is too wide/tall is downscaled/rejected (LiteRT/ML Kit input size limits).\n\nSearch hints: grep for \"manual\", \"selection\", \"crop\", \"Rect\", \"aspect\", \"minWidth\", \"maxWidth\", \"coerceIn\", \"isAcceptableCyrillicOcrText\", \"dictionaryCoverage\", \"region\", \"overlay\".\n\nReturn: concise list (ranked by likelihood) of file:line + the constraint/check + the numeric threshold and what it rejects.", "subagent_type": "explore"}, "error": "Task cancelled", "metadata": {"parentSessionId": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "sessionId": "ses_ec98bbfa5ffeOi1A9NPNpJ8pDP", "model": {"modelID": "big-pickle", "providerID": "opencode"}}, "time": {"start": 1791914950750, "end": 1791915933682}}, "id": "prt_1367433be0014pV6QZQyYkNIHo", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136740664002noSSiqmqT8lo2U"}]}, {"info": {"role": "user", "time": {"created": 1791915942309}, "agent": "build", "model": {"providerID": "opencode", "modelID": "big-pickle"}, "summary": {"diffs": []}, "id": "msg_1368361a5001ciimKtqfPBhiNO", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"type": "text", "text": "ну что там", "id": "prt_1368361b2001tb1I7RpWfsuq8o", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1368361a5001ciimKtqfPBhiNO"}]}, {"info": {"parentID": "msg_1368361a5001ciimKtqfPBhiNO", "role": "assistant", "mode": "build", "agent": "build", "path": {"cwd": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code", "root": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"total": 152592, "input": 11896, "output": 738, "reasoning": 6838, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 133120}}, "modelID": "big-pickle", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1791915944664, "completed": 1791916020987}, "finish": "tool-calls", "id": "msg_136836ad8002afuZOfLmAEt0O3", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_1368385f5001RxztnqhF5UprJ7", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136836ad8002afuZOfLmAEt0O3"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "The user asks \"ну что там\" = \"so what's there / what's up\". Two of three explore tasks completed; the third (manual region OCR selection) was cancelled. I need to give a status update concisely and continue.\n\nLet me summarize findings and next actions. Given the huge scope, I should report what I found and propose the concrete fixes, especially the most impactful ones directly tied to the user's complaints:\n\n1. Slow UI startup — found real culprits:\n   - `Migrator.awaitAndRelease()` runBlocking on main (MainActivity.kt:179).\n   - `AppModule` \"async init\" uses main executor (AppModule.kt:151-160) → builds Database/NetworkHelper/ExtensionManager (loads all extensions via runBlocking)/DownloadManager on main.\n   - `OcrScreenshotBuffer.init` and `OcrVocabulary.configure` sync file I/O in App.onCreate.\n   \n2. OCR first-call no model chooser + auto-download/init slowing phone:\n   - `ensureOcrModelsInstalled()` auto-downloads 21MB cyrillic pack at startup.\n   - `warmupOcr()` on reader open loads 3 TFLite models eagerly.\n   - No first-run engine chooser.\n\n3. Dictionary 3M — my change reduced APK ~19MB but runtime still builds full 3M HashSet on first OCR → hang. User wants chunked.\n\n4. Manual region selection — task cancelled, need to investigate.\n\nI'm now in build mode. But this is a very large set of changes. I should prioritize and probably tackle the dictionary (issue 3) first since it's directly related to the current work and is the \"hangs hard\" complaint, plus fix the startup main-thread issues (issue 1) which are clear wins, and the OCR first-run (issue 2) needs product decisions (a chooser dialog) — that's bigger.\n\nGiven the user's frustration and \"ну что там\", let me give a concise status and then continue working. I should not dump everything. Let me report key findings briefly and state what I'll fix, then start with the highest-impact low-risk fixes.\n\nActually, the user is likely asking \"what's the status\". Let me answer concisely and continue implementation. I think the best is to fix the concrete performance bugs:\n\nPriority order:\n1. **Dictionary chunked / no hang** (directly requested; relates to current change). Rework RuWordList to not build 3M String objects; use memory-efficient structure. This also helps the \"first OCR hangs\".\n2. **Startup main-thread fixes** (issue 1): move `OcrVocabulary.configure`, `OcrScreenshotBuffer.init` off main; fix AppModule main-executor; make Migrator not runBlocking on main. But these are more invasive and risky.\n3. **First-run OCR chooser** (issue 2): bigger product work.\n4. **Manual region** (issue 4): need investigation.\n\nThis is a lot. I should be honest that I'll do them incrementally. Let me start with the dictionary rework, since it's the most tied to what we did and clearly requested.\n\nBut wait — I need to decide the chunked design. Let me think about what \"chunks\" means practically and what won't regress speed.\n\nCurrent: `RuWordList.upper: Set<String>` = HashSet of 3,014,492 uppercase strings. Built once lazily. Memory ~300-400MB. That's the hang (GC + allocation). The user says use \"чанками\" (chunks).\n\nDesign options:\nA. **Byte-backed sorted dictionary + binary search**: load file as `ByteArray` (71MB), search a candidate by scanning. To binary search by lines, need line offsets (3M ints = 12MB) or scan. Membership test must be fast (called many times during DP segmentation). Binary search over 3M lines = ~22 comparisons; each comparison reads a line substring. If we store the whole file as bytes and line offsets, each contains() converts candidate to bytes and binary searches. Converting candidate (uppercase String) to bytes each call adds cost, but candidate lengths are short. This is ~O(log n * wordlen). Could be slower than HashSet O(1) but much less memory. During splitGluedRun there can be many lookups (DP over substrings) — could be thousands per caption. Binary search of 22 steps each with byte compare of ~10 bytes: ~220 byte ops vs O(1) hash. Maybe 5-20x slower per lookup but acceptable? Risky for \"speed\".\n\nB. **Chunked by first letter / hash bucket**: partition dictionary into N chunks (e.g., 33 Cyrillic letters or 256 hash buckets), each chunk a `Set<String>` (or sorted array). Load only needed chunks on demand, cache. During a caption, lookups span few first letters → loads few chunks. Memory stays low. Membership is O(1) within loaded chunk. Load cost per chunk = (3M/N) inserts; with N=256, ~12k words per chunk, fast. This is genuinely \"chunked\" and fast. \n\nBut lookups need to map a candidate to a chunk: first char (or hash) → chunk file. If chunk by first letter, we'd have ~33 files, but distribution uneven (some letters huge). Better: fixed-size chunks by line ranges (e.g., 50k words per chunk, 61 chunks), and determine which chunk by first letter via an index (first-letter → chunk range). Since sorted, the chunk containing first letter X is determined by scanning an index of first words per chunk. \n\nSimplest robust: build an index at load time? No—avoid loading. We can store a tiny index file (or compute chunk boundaries by reading only the first line of each chunk). Actually, to find the chunk for a word, we binary search over chunk-boundary first-words; but that requires reading those boundary words (cheap, 61 reads). Or store an index asset mapping letter→chunk.\n\nHmm, but this complicates the generator and runtime significantly, and correctness risk (missing words → OCR regression). The user cares about no regression.\n\nC. **Single sorted `Array<String>`**? Still 3M String objects (~150MB). Better than HashSet (~300MB) and faster to build (sorted file → array via split). Actually `File.readLines()` allocates 3M strings anyway. Memory ~200MB. Loading via `readLines()` still creates the 3M strings but avoids hash insert. Hmm.\n\nD. **Load as a single String and use a compact hash set of integers** (open addressing over a `IntArray`/`LongArray` storing hashes + offsets). Membership: compute hash of candidate, probe. Backed by one big `ByteArray` (71MB) + `IntArray` offsets (12MB). Memory ~85MB, fast contains (hash). Build = parse once into arrays (no String objects). This is the best of both: low memory, O(1)-ish, load is a single pass. But implementing a correct custom hash map is error-prone and could regress.\n\nGiven constraints (no perf/ocr regression, avoid hangs), option B (chunked by first letter) directly matches the user's ask (\"чанками\"), keeps HashSet semantics per chunk, and caps memory. But it changes the asset format and generator significantly.\n\nHmm, wait. Let me reconsider the actual reported symptom: \"он использует тот словарь на 3млн чанками а не целиком а то виснет жестко и не понятно от чего\". The hang is likely the one-time build of the 3M HashSet (hundreds of MB allocation → GC storm / possible OOM) on first OCR. The user wants it to not do that all at once.\n\nChunking by first letter: during a single caption, the words have varied first letters but typically a handful. However DP segmentation tests arbitrary substrings — the substrings' first letters are within the caption's letters. So maybe 5-15 distinct first letters per caption. Loading those chunks on demand = a few thousand inserts each. Good. Subsequent captions reuse cached chunks. Memory bounded by number of distinct letters encountered (~33 max → could reach full dictionary over a long session, but that's gradual, not a spike). \n\nThis is a good design. But it requires the asset to be pre-split into per-first-letter chunks, OR the runtime reads a range of the sorted file. Since the file is sorted, per-letter ranges are contiguous! We can compute ranges if we know, for each first letter, the start line index. We can generate an index in the asset or compute by scanning.\n\nBut reading a \"chunk\" = read lines from offset to offset. With a plain text asset, we can't random-access by line offset easily. We'd need line offsets index (3M entries) or scan from start (O(n)). Better: generate separate chunk files per first letter? That's 33+ assets. Or a single file + an offset index at the top.\n\nHmm, this is getting complex. Let me consider a simpler, effective approach:\n\n**Sorted String array + binary search, single `CharArray`/`String`**: \n- Load asset as one big `String` (71MB, plus String's char[] = UTF-16 → 140MB! since Java String is UTF-16). Ouch — 71MB UTF-8 becomes 140MB UTF-16. Bad. Use `ByteArray` (71MB) instead.\n- Build an `IntArray` of line-start offsets (3M ints = 12MB) via a single pass.\n- `contains(word)`: binary search using offsets, comparing bytes. No per-word String allocation. Memory ~83MB. Load = single read + offset scan (fast, no 3M objects). \n- Performance: binary search ~22 steps; each step decode a line from bytes to compare. We can compare byte-by-byte to the candidate's UTF-8 bytes. Candidate strings are already uppercase; encode once per contains call. This is maybe slower than hash but acceptable and far better than an OOM/hang.\n\nActually, even simpler and fast: since we only need membership and the file is sorted, use the ByteArray + offsets binary search. This avoids the hash entirely and the memory spike.\n\nBut is binary search \"chunked\"? Not really. The user said chunks. But the real goal is \"don't build all at once / don't hang\". Binary-search-over-bytes loads the whole file (71MB) in one read but doesn't allocate 3M objects → no hang from object churn; it's a single bulk read.\n\nHmm, but 71MB ByteArray allocation is also a spike (though one allocation, fast; GC handles big arrays in one go, likely in native/off-heap-ish? Actually Java heap). 71MB is fine on modern devices.\n\nActually, the cleanest \"chunk\" interpretation that's simple: **lazy per-first-letter loading from a single sorted asset using a precomputed offset index**, where each chunk is a HashSet. This is more code.\n\nGiven time and risk, I think the pragmatic best is:\n- Keep the asset (plain text, sorted).\n- Runtime: load lazily a **byte array + line offset index**, and do binary search. Memory ~83MB, no 3M String objects, single-pass load. This eliminates the hang and is much lighter than the 300MB HashSet.\n- This is a big improvement and low correctness risk (same word set).\n\nBut binary search per lookup might be slower than current HashSet. During OCR DP, could be many lookups. Let me estimate: splitGluedRun likely does DP over a run of length L, testing O(L^2) substrings in the worst case, but with MAX_WORD_LEN 24 and pruning, maybe O(L*24). For L=100, ~2400 lookups. Binary search 22 steps each → 52k comparisons per caption. Cheap (<1ms). Fine. Actually HashSet would be ~2400 hashes. So binary search maybe 20x more work but still sub-ms. Acceptable. And we only need this on first OCR (dictionary now at startup? no, lazy).\n\nHmm wait, but there's a subtlety: current code uses `RuWordList.upper` as a `Set<String>` in `OcrTextCleaner.kt:468` (`up in RuWordList.upper`) and `OcrVocabulary.kt:137`. If I change `upper` to not be a `Set`, I must update those call sites to call e.g. `RuWordList.contains(up)`. That's fine (2 sites).\n\nLet me go with: `RuWordList.contains(word: String): Boolean` backed by ByteArray + IntArray offsets, binary search.\n\nActually, let me reconsider — implementing robust binary search over UTF-8 lines with offsets. The file is sorted alphabetically in Python's `sorted()` order = Unicode code point order. Russian uppercase letters are contiguous in Unicode (А..Я, Ё). Python sorts by code point, and my `sorted(lines)` uses Python str comparison = code point. The Kotlin `contains` must binary search in the SAME order to find entries. Python sorts Unicode strings by code point; comparing UTF-8 bytes lexicographically gives the SAME order as code point comparison (UTF-8 preserves code point order). So byte-wise binary search over UTF-8 lines works. \n\nBut there's a catch: are all lines pure Cyrillic (so no multi-byte ordering surprises)? There are hyphenated words (`-` = U+002D) and maybe `ё`. Code point order vs UTF-8 byte order: UTF-8 byte order = code point order for valid UTF-8. `-` (0x2D) sorts before Cyrillic. Python's sorted put them accordingly. Byte comparison matches. Good.\n\nSo the plan:\n- `upper` API replaced by `contains(word)` (or keep `upper` as a lazy `Set`? No—that defeats the purpose).\n- But other code imports `RuWordList.upper` (2 sites). I'll change them.\n\nHmm, actually, wait. Let me reconsider whether this is worth the complexity/risk right now, versus a simpler chunked approach.\n\nAlternative simplest approach that satisfies \"not all at once\": load the dictionary in the background at startup (not lazily on first OCR), so the hang doesn't happen during OCR. But it still builds 3M objects → memory spike, just moved to startup (bad for the UI slowness issue #1!). Not good.\n\nI think binary-search bytes is the right call: low memory, no hang.\n\nBut honestly, the scope here is enormous (4 issues). Let me focus and communicate. Let me give the user a status now and propose to fix in order, starting with the dictionary (since it's concrete) and the clear startup main-thread bugs. I shouldn't try to do all 4 in one massive change without confirmation on the product-level ones (first-run chooser, manual selection).\n\nLet me respond with a concise status and my plan, then start implementing the dictionary rework.\n\nActually the user asked \"ну что там\" — they want to know progress. Let me answer briefly and then continue with work (build mode). I'll implement the highest-value fix now: the dictionary (no hang) + the startup main-thread fixes.\n\nBut implementing startup fixes (#1) is invasive and needs care. Let me do the dictionary first (most concrete, tied to prior work), then do the clear main-thread I/O moves (OcrVocabulary + OcrScreenshotBuffer off main, and fix AppModule main-executor to IO, and Migrator not blocking main). Those are relatively safe.\n\nHmm, but the AppModule `getMainExecutor` change: the comment says \"asynchronously init expensive components for faster cold start\". Maybe they intentionally used main executor but that's a bug. Changing to a background thread/executor could affect thread-safety of Injekt singletons. Risky. Let me be careful — maybe the safe subset is moving OcrScreenshotBuffer.init and OcrVocabulary.configure off main.\n\nActually, let me reconsider priorities given effort/risk:\n- Dictionary rework: directly requested, concrete. DO.\n- Startup I/O off main (OcrScreenshotBuffer, OcrVocabulary): safe-ish, helps #1. DO.\n- AppModule main-executor and Migrator runBlocking: risky, architectural. Propose, maybe do carefully.\n- First-run OCR chooser: product decision, larger. Propose.\n- Manual region constraints: need the cancelled investigation. Investigate then fix.\n\nGiven the user's tone (\"ну что там\"), they want visible progress. Let me give a concise status of findings and then implement the dictionary rework now.\n\nLet me answer concisely and start.\n\nWait, I should be mindful: the release APK build I started earlier was aborted by the user, and the previous spotless check was also aborted. My current working tree has the asset-based RuWordList (HashSet full load). I'm about to rework it to byte-backed binary search. Let me do that.\n\nLet me design the new RuWordList:\n\n```kotlin\npackage mihon.data.ocr\n\nimport android.content.Context\nimport java.io.File\nimport java.io.InputStream\nimport logcat.LogPriority\nimport tachiyomi.core.common.util.system.logcat\n\nobject RuWordList {\n    private const val ASSET_PATH = \"ocr/ru_wordlist.txt\"\n\n    @Volatile private var opener: (() -> InputStream)? = null\n    fun configure(context: Context) { opener = { context.assets.open(ASSET_PATH) } }\n\n    // Byte-backed sorted dictionary: single UTF-8 buffer + line start offsets.\n    // Не создаёт 3 млн String-объектов (это и вешало телефон), память ~80 МБ,\n    // загрузка — один массовый read.\n    private class Dict(val bytes: ByteArray, val starts: IntArray) {\n        fun contains(word: String): Boolean {\n            // encode word as UTF-8\n            var lo = 0; var hi = starts.size - 1\n            while (lo <= hi) {\n                val mid = (lo + hi) ushr 1\n                val cmp = compareLine(bytes, starts, mid, word)\n                when {\n                    cmp < 0 -> lo = mid + 1\n                    cmp > 0 -> hi = mid - 1\n                    else -> return true\n                }\n            }\n            return false\n        }\n    }\n    ...\n}\n```\n\ncompareLine: compare bytes of the line (from starts[mid] to next newline or starts[mid+1]) with the UTF-8 bytes of `word`. Need to encode `word` to UTF-8 bytes once per contains (allocate small array). Line end: starts[mid+1]-1 (since each line ends with '\\n'), and starts has size = number of lines (maybe +1 sentinel = bytes.size). Let me build starts with N+1 entries where starts[N] = bytes.size (sentinel).\n\nParsing the asset: read all bytes, then scan for '\\n' to fill starts. But `InputStream.readBytes()` gives the whole file (71MB). Then count lines. We can do a single pass.\n\nWait, building `starts` requires knowing line count first (to size IntArray). We can count '\\n' in one pass, allocate, then fill in a second pass, or use a growable IntArray (3M inserts into IntArray via manual growth). Two passes over 71MB is fine (~ms). Or use an ArrayList<Int>? boxing bad. Let me count lines then fill.\n\nActually simpler: parse with an `IntArray` built by scanning; since max lines unknown, count first.\n\nEncoding word to UTF-8 each contains() call allocates. Could avoid by comparing char-by-char against bytes: decode bytes to chars on the fly. Since words are ASCII+Cyrillic (BMP), UTF-8 decoding is straightforward. But simpler: `word.toByteArray(Charsets.UTF_8)` — small allocation. During thousands of lookups, that's fine.\n\nActually even better: we can avoid per-call allocation by comparing char-by-char with manual UTF-8 encode of each char. But let's keep it simple; allocation of ~10 bytes × thousands is negligible.\n\nBinary search compare: \n- line range [start, end) where end = starts[mid+1]-1 (excluding '\\n'), or if sentinel use bytes.size (and last line may end with '\\n').\n- Compare lexicographically byte vs UTF-8(word).\n\nLet me implement `compare(bytes, lineStart, lineEnd, word)`:\n```\nvar i = lineStart\nvar j = 0\nwhile (i < lineEnd && j < word.length) {\n    val b = bytes[i].toInt() and 0xFF\n    // decode next UTF-8 char from bytes\n    ... compare with word[j]\n}\n```\nDecoding is annoying. Alternative: encode word once to ByteArray `wb`, then compare bytes directly:\n```\nvar i = lineStart; var k = 0\nwhile (i < lineEnd && k < wb.size) {\n    val cb = bytes[i].toInt() and 0xFF\n    val wbb = wb[k].toInt() and 0xFF\n    if (cb != wbb) return cb - wbb\n    i++; k++\n}\nreturn (lineEnd - lineStart) - wb.size\n```\nSince both are UTF-8, byte comparison = code point order. \n\nBut wait: binary search order must match Python sorted order. Python sorted by code point = byte order. And `wb` from Kotlin `uppercase()` of the candidate — must match the asset's uppercase form. The asset is generated with Python `.upper()`. Kotlin `.uppercase()` and Python `.upper()` for Cyrillic produce the same (both map а→А, ё→Ё). Edge: Turkish locale in Kotlin `.uppercase()` (default locale). Existing code used `word.uppercase()`, so parity. Actually to be safe, use `word.uppercase()` (default locale) same as before? The asset is fixed; candidate must match. If device locale is Turkish, `i`.uppercase() = \"İ\" vs asset \"I\"—but asset is Cyrillic, no Latin `i` (except... seeds are Cyrillic). So fine.\n\nHmm, but there might be Latin in the dictionary? Earlier extraction showed all forms are Cyrillic (3,014,492 cyr-only) plus single letters, no Latin. Good.\n\ncontains() should handle empty/blank → false.\n\nNow, memory: bytes=71MB, starts=3M*4=12MB → ~83MB. Better than ~300MB. Load time: read 71MB (inflate from APK) + count + fill. Maybe 0.3-0.8s. Still a one-time cost but much less GC pressure.\n\nBut the user explicitly wants \"chunks\". Binary search isn't chunked, but it removes the hang. Hmm. Let me reconsider whether to implement true chunking to honor the request.\n\nTrue chunking design (per first-letter):\n- Asset is sorted. Precompute for each distinct first char (or first 2 chars) the byte range. Store an index (e.g., a small JSON/text with char→startLine). Runtime reads lines only for the needed slice.\n- But random access to a line slice in a plain file requires the line-offset index anyway (12MB) OR separate chunk files.\n\nAlternative true-chunking without offsets: split into separate asset files per first-letter: `ocr/ru/А.txt`, `ocr/ru/Б.txt`, ... (33 files). Runtime loads a file's lines into a HashSet lazily by first letter of the candidate. `contains(word)`: chunkFor(firstChar(word)).contains(word). Each chunk HashSet small (largest letter maybe ~500k words → still 500k objects, ~50MB; acceptable but not tiny). Better split by two letters prefix? Overkill.\n\nHmm, the first-letter distribution in Russian is uneven; \"П\" and \"С\" are huge (~300k each). Still far less than 3M at once, and only a few letters loaded per session. This is genuinely chunked and matches the request, and keeps HashSet O(1) lookups (no perf regression). The cost: many small asset files (33) + generator change + a fallback.\n\nBut is loading per-letter chunks going to accumulate to all 33 over a long reading session (→ same 3M in memory eventually)? Possibly, but gradually and only for letters actually encountered; and we could evict (LRU) or cap. Simpler: not evict — gradual growth is much less janky than one 3M spike. Or we could cap to N chunks with LRU. Overkill.\n\nGiven the user's explicit \"чанками\", I lean toward the per-first-letter chunk files + HashSet. It's simpler to reason about and preserves O(1) lookups.\n\nBut wait — `RuWordList.upper` is `Set<String>`; call sites do `up in RuWordList.upper`. I'd change to `RuWordList.contains(up)`.\n\nHmm, but there's a complication: `OcrTextCleaner` may also use the dictionary for `looksLikeDictionaryRamp` etc.? Let me check all usages beyond the 2. Earlier grep found only 2 usages of `.upper`. Good.\n\nLet me also consider: the DP segmentation might need to test a substring; first char of substring = some char in the caption. Loading by first char works.\n\nDecision: implement per-first-letter chunks. Generator writes `data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru/<CHAR>.txt` for each first character (using a filename-safe encoding, e.g., the char itself is Cyrillic — filenames with Cyrillic are fine on Android? Asset names with non-ASCII might be problematic. Better use a safe key: hex code point, e.g., `ru/041f.txt` for П). Or index file listing buckets.\n\nSimpler: one asset file per bucket named by a URL-safe key = first char's Unicode code point hex. Runtime computes bucket key from first char.\n\nActually, even simpler and robust: keep a **single** asset but also a tiny **index** asset with bucket boundaries, and load slices by reading the single asset with a `BufferedInputStream` skipping to the bucket offset (byte offset known from index). Since the file is sorted, each first-letter bucket is a contiguous byte range. The index maps first char → (byteStart, byteEnd). Runtime opens the asset, skips byteStart, reads until byteEnd into a HashSet. This is chunked (only needed letter's lines), single file, no 3M offsets. \n\nBut opening+skipping on an inflated asset stream re-inflates from the start each time (skip on a deflated stream still decompresses the skipped bytes!). That's expensive per bucket (up to 71MB decompress to skip). Bad.\n\nUnless we load the whole asset bytes once (71MB) and slice in memory — then it's basically the byte-array approach with per-letter HashSets built lazily from slices. That's: bytes 71MB + per-letter HashSet of loaded buckets. Memory could exceed the pure-hashset approach if all loaded. Hmm.\n\nOK, I think the cleanest to honor \"chunks\" AND avoid the decompress issue is **separate small asset files per bucket** (compress each independently in APK). Load only the buckets used. Let me do that.\n\nNumber of buckets: by first char. Let me count distinct first chars in the dictionary to size it. Likely ~33 (all Cyrillic uppercase + hyphen). Each file deflates small. APK total still ~sum of compressed buckets ≈ 8-11MB (same as single file, maybe slightly worse due to per-file deflate overhead). Fine.\n\nFilename: use a bucket id. To avoid non-ASCII filenames, encode first char as its hex code: e.g. `ocr/ru_words/0410.txt` for 'А'. Runtime: `ASSET_DIR + \"/%04X.txt\".format(ch.code)`. Simple and safe.\n\nGenerator: write each bucket.\n\nBut then `EXPECTED_FORMS` capacity isn't known per bucket; just use default HashSet() growth, fine.\n\nRuntime:\n```kotlin\nobject RuWordList {\n    private const val DIR = \"ocr/ru_words\"\n    private val cache = HashMap<Char, Set<String>>()  // guarded\n    private val lock = Any()\n    @Volatile private var assets: AssetManager? = null\n    private val testDir: File? ...\n\n    fun configure(context: Context) { assets = context.assets }\n\n    private fun bucket(ch: Char): Set<String>? {\n        synchronized(lock) { cache[ch]?.let { return it } }\n        val words = loadBucket(ch) ?: return null\n        synchronized(lock) { return cache.getOrPut(ch) { words } }\n    }\n\n    fun contains(word: String): Boolean {\n        if (word.isEmpty()) return false\n        val ch = word[0]\n        val set = bucket(ch) ?: return false\n        return set.contains(word)\n    }\n}\n```\n\nloadBucket reads the asset file for ch; if missing, return null (and maybe remember negative to avoid repeated open attempts — cache emptySet). For test fallback, read from filesystem dir.\n\nThis is clean and truly chunked. Memory grows only as letters are used.\n\nBut hold on: is this over-engineering vs the binary-search approach? The user explicitly asked for chunks and complained about hangs. Per-letter chunks directly address it and keep O(1) lookups (no perf regression). I'll go with it.\n\nHmm, but wait: the buckets might be uneven and a single letter could still be ~800k words (e.g., \"П\"). Building an 800k HashSet is ~80MB and ~0.1-0.3s — acceptable, not a 3M spike. Could sub-bucket by first two chars for smoothness, but that's more files. First-letter is likely enough. Let me check the distribution to be safe.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the whole thing once more. This is a LOT of work and risk for a behavior the user may accept differently. Given the user is impatient, maybe I should present the plan and get a quick confirmation before a big refactor. But they already said \"нужно чтобы он использовал тот словарь чанками\" — that's a directive. So implement chunking.\n\nBut before coding, let me measure the per-first-letter distribution to choose bucket granularity.\n\nLet me also handle the other issues. Given the volume, I'll:\n- Respond with a status summary.\n- Implement dictionary chunking.\n- Implement safe startup I/O offloading.\n- Investigate manual region constraints.\n- Propose the first-run chooser (needs UX decision).\n\nGiven \"ну что там\", let me first reply concisely with findings, then continue. Actually, I can reply and immediately act in the same turn. Let me do the analysis of bucket distribution and start implementing.\n\nLet me not over-plan in text; the user wants results. Let me report the diagnosis briefly and begin implementing the dictionary chunking + startup I/O offload.\n\nLet me first compute the first-char distribution.\n\nActually, I realize I should confirm what the user wants me to do right now given limited turns. They said \"ну что там\" — I'll give a crisp status: found the causes, here's what I'll fix first (dictionary chunking + startup main-thread I/O), and I'm doing it. Then implement.\n\nLet me compute distribution and implement.\n\nOne more consideration: The release build verification (APK size) is still pending. We know ~19MB savings from the DEX→asset change. I'll mention it.\n\nLet me get the bucket distribution.", "time": {"start": 1791915951737, "end": 1791916000837}, "id": "prt_136838679001XIy5TcPebCJ9Mj", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136836ad8002afuZOfLmAEt0O3"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Статус: две из трёх разведок завершились, картина ясная. Третью (ручное выделение) перезапущу. Ключевые находки:\n\n**Тормоза старта UI (v2.0.0):**\n1. `Migrator.awaitAndRelease()` — `runBlocking` прямо на главном потоке (MainActivity.kt:179), плюс первые миграции идут на main из-за `CoroutineStart.UNDISPATCHED` (MigrationJobFactory.kt:22).\n2. `AppModule.kt:151-160` «асинхронная» инициализация на самом деле `getMainExecutor` → строит БД, `NetworkHelper`, `ExtensionManager` (грузит **все расширения** через `runBlocking`, ExtensionLoader.kt:166) на UI-потоке.\n3. `OcrScreenshotBuffer.init` (App.kt:160) и `OcrVocabulary.configure` (App.kt:148) — синхронный диск/JSON на main.\n4. `warmupOcr()` при открытии читалки грузит 3 TFLite + 2 словаря (CyrillicOcrEngine.kt:163).\n\n**OCR первый вызов:** движок тихо дефолтится в `CYRILLIC` (OcrRepositoryImpl.kt:40), chooser отсутствует; на старте автоматически качается ~21 МБ `cyrillic_ocr` (App.kt:364).\n\n**Словарь 3 млн:** в релизе это `classes4.dex` 140 МБ распакованных / 30 МБ в APK; мой перевод в ассет даёт ~19 МБ, но рантайм всё равно строит весь `HashSet` на 3 млн сразу — оттуда зависание.\n\nСейчас: переделываю словарь на чанки и убираю тяжёлый I/O со главного потока. Сначала посмотрю распределение по буквам, чтобы выбрать размер чанка.", "time": {"start": 1791916000923, "end": 1791916005104}, "id": "prt_13684469a001n8UmKDCGnTXtGe", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136836ad8002afuZOfLmAEt0O3"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "bash", "callID": "call_00_x1td45un13f6hkheqxd1sdsn", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"command": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code && python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom collections import Counter\nc = Counter()\nwith open('data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    for line in f:\n        w = line.rstrip('\\n')\n        if w:\n            c[w[0]] += 1\ntot = sum(c.values())\nprint(\"total:\", tot, \"distinct first chars:\", len(c))\nfor ch, n in c.most_common(12):\n    print(repr(ch), n)\nprint(\"min:\", c.most_common()[-5:])\n# bucket by first two chars count\nc2 = Counter()\nwith open('data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    for line in f:\n        w = line.rstrip('\\n')\n        if w:\n            c2[w[:2]] += 1\nprint(\"distinct 2-char prefixes:\", len(c2), \"max bucket:\", c2.most_common(3))\nEOF"}, "output": "total: 3014492 distinct first chars: 30\n'П' 555137\n'С' 237621\n'О' 230517\n'Н' 223244\n'В' 213952\n'А' 169890\n'Р' 158953\n'З' 144377\n'К' 138880\n'Д' 119581\n'М' 109244\n'Б' 105203\nmin: [('Я', 8213), ('Щ', 4484), ('Ю', 4359), ('Й', 1278), ('Ы', 6)]\ndistinct 2-char prefixes: 643 max bucket: [('ПО', 213751), ('ПР', 178727), ('ЗА', 124184)]\n", "metadata": {"output": "total: 3014492 distinct first chars: 30\n'П' 555137\n'С' 237621\n'О' 230517\n'Н' 223244\n'В' 213952\n'А' 169890\n'Р' 158953\n'З' 144377\n'К' 138880\n'Д' 119581\n'М' 109244\n'Б' 105203\nmin: [('Я', 8213), ('Щ', 4484), ('Ю', 4359), ('Й', 1278), ('Ы', 6)]\ndistinct 2-char prefixes: 643 max bucket: [('ПО', 213751), ('ПР', 178727), ('ЗА', 124184)]\n", "exit": 0, "truncated": false}, "title": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code && python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom collections import Counter\nc = Counter()\nwith open('data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    for line in f:\n        w = line.rstrip('\\n')\n        if w:\n            c[w[0]] += 1\ntot = sum(c.values())\nprint(\"total:\", tot, \"distinct first chars:\", len(c))\nfor ch, n in c.most_common(12):\n    print(repr(ch), n)\nprint(\"min:\", c.most_common()[-5:])\n# bucket by first two chars count\nc2 = Counter()\nwith open('data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    for line in f:\n        w = line.rstrip('\\n')\n        if w:\n            c2[w[:2]] += 1\nprint(\"distinct 2-char prefixes:\", len(c2), \"max bucket:\", c2.most_common(3))\nEOF", "time": {"start": 1791916005075, "end": 1791916019960}}, "id": "prt_13684512b001vPQrkg3lagJf9B", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136836ad8002afuZOfLmAEt0O3"}, {"reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-finish", "tokens": {"total": 152592, "input": 11896, "output": 738, "reasoning": 6838, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 133120}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_1368492f8001I1qXJXUcFLD2CR", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136836ad8002afuZOfLmAEt0O3"}]}, {"info": {"role": "user", "model": {"providerID": "opencode", "modelID": "big-pickle"}, "agent": "build", "time": {"created": 1791916020999}, "summary": {"diffs": []}, "id": "msg_136849507001NbTqEUuQNU11br", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"type": "compaction", "auto": true, "overflow": false, "tail_start_id": "msg_1368361a5001ciimKtqfPBhiNO", "id": "prt_13684950e00172u5lci72TZ8FU", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136849507001NbTqEUuQNU11br"}]}, {"info": {"role": "assistant", "parentID": "msg_136849507001NbTqEUuQNU11br", "mode": "compaction", "agent": "compaction", "summary": true, "path": {"cwd": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code", "root": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"total": 90095, "input": 86518, "output": 2038, "reasoning": 1539, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 0}}, "modelID": "big-pickle", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1791916027353, "completed": 1791916056218}, "finish": "stop", "id": "msg_13684add9001gOhKucbovDh4ck", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_13684d0b4001lggaZCM44jjyGM", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13684add9001gOhKucbovDh4ck"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "Let me analyze the conversation and produce the structured summary.\n\nKey facts:\n- Repo: /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code — Android app \"Yomikai\" (manga reader with OCR), Kotlin, multi-module Gradle.\n- package applicationId app.yomikai, namespace eu.kanade.tachiyomi\n- User is Russian-speaking; responds in Russian.\n- Original issue: TAPK (ru.trashbox.tapk) stack trace: `java.io.IOException: Failed to allocate 87103556 because only 0 allocatable` at RootlessSaiPackageInstaller.install line 94 / session.openWrite.\n- User: \"последний релиз версия 2.0.0 не устанавливается\" (latest release v2.0.0 doesn't install).\n- Confirmed: released APK `yomikai-v2.0.0.apk` size = 87,103,556 bytes exactly (matches crash). Downloaded to /tmp/opencode/yomikai-v2.0.0.apk.\n- Root cause: installd ENOSPC — device has 0 free space to stage 87MB APK.\n- Dictionary: RuWordList — 3,014,492 Russian wordforms, hardcoded in 603 Kotlin files `data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/RuWordListPart*.kt` (~90MB source, ~3M lines). In released APK: classes4.dex = 140,804,312 bytes uncompressed → 30,163,093 bytes compressed. Replacing with asset: raw text 71,110,950 bytes → compressed to 11,340,327 bytes in APK. Expected saving ~18.8MB → new release ~68.3MB.\n- User chose \"GZ-ассет в APK (Recommended)\" option.\n- User caveat: \"если ничего по скорости не критично то да а если чтото ухудшиться то не надо\" — only if no speed regression.\n\nChanges made (working tree, uncommitted):\n1. Generated asset `data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt` — 3,014,492 uppercase sorted forms, LF, 71,110,950 bytes.\n2. Rewrote `data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/RuWordList.kt`: object with `ASSET_PATH = \"ocr/ru_wordlist.txt\"`, `EXPECTED_FORMS = 3_014_492`, `TEST_SOURCE_CANDIDATES = listOf(\"src/main/assets/$ASSET_PATH\", \"data/src/main/assets/$ASSET_PATH\")`, `configure(context)`, `openSource()`, `upper: Set<String> by lazy(LazyThreadSafetyMode.SYNCHRONIZED)` building HashSet with exact capacity, logcat WARN if asset missing.\n3. Deleted 603 `RuWordListPart*.kt`.\n4. Wired `mihon.data.ocr.RuWordList.configure(applicationContext)` in `app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/App.kt` after OcrVocabulary.configure (~line 148-156).\n5. Updated `scripts/gen_ruwordlist.py` to emit the asset (write_asset), removed write_parts/sync_parts_list/repo_forms, REPO_OCR_DIR/RULIST_KT/PART_SIZE constants, `import re`; added ASSET_REL; main() calls write_asset(repo, forms).\n6. `gradle.properties`: kotlin.daemon.jvmargs from -Xmx7g back to -Xmx3g, comment about RuWordList removed.\n\nVerification done:\n- `./gradlew :data:compileDebugKotlin` succeeded on 3g.\n- `./gradlew :data:testDebugUnitTest --tests \"mihon.data.ocr.*\"` passed; OcrTextCleanerTest 37/37, OcrTextCleanerUserDictTest 8/8, 17 test classes no failures.\n- `./gradlew :app:assembleDebug` succeeded → app-arm64-v8a-debug.apk = 107,767,032 bytes (103MB). Asset inside APK: `assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt` 71,110,950 stored → Defl:N 11,340,327 (compressed).\n\nBlocked/aborted:\n- User aborted `./gradlew :app:assembleRelease` (twice? once) — release APK size not measured.\n- User aborted `./gradlew :data:spotlessCheck :app:spotlessCheck`.\n\nNew user feedback (4 issues about v2.0.0):\n1. Very slow UI loading (\"очень медленно прогружается интерфейс\").\n2. On first OCR invocation, doesn't prompt to choose \"voices\"/models, auto-selects, heavily slows phone.\n3. Dictionary (3M) should be used in chunks, not entirely — otherwise hangs hard (\"виснет жестко\").\n4. Manual text region selection capturing frames/speech bubbles mostly returns no result due to width/length constraints.\n\nInvestigation state: 2 explore tasks completed (startup slowness, OCR engine selection flow); 3rd explore task (manual region selection) was cancelled when conversation ended.\n\nTodos created:\n- Диагностика: медленный старт UI v2.0.0 (in_progress)\n- Диагностика: OCR первый вызов (pending)\n- Словарь 3млн: чанки (pending)\n- Ручное выделение области (pending)\n\nKey facts from explore:\n- OcrPreferences pref key `pref_ocr_model` default `OcrModel.CYRILLIC`. OcrRepositoryImpl.kt engine selection lines.\n- OcrPlugins.kt registry.\n- App.kt startup items.\n\nLet me capture important file paths:\n- data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/RuWordList.kt\n- data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt\n- scripts/gen_ruwordlist.py\n- app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/App.kt\n- app/build.gradle.kts (line 220-221 androidResources noCompress tflite/bin; splits arm64-v8a only)\n- gradle.properties\n- data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/OcrTextCleaner.kt (line 468 uses RuWordList.upper)\n- data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/OcrVocabulary.kt (line 137)\n- data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/OcrRepositoryImpl.kt (engine selection)\n- data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/OcrPlugins.kt\n- app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/extension/installer/PackageInstallerInstaller.kt (unrelated, repo's own)\n\nNow format the summary.\n\nNext move: address dictionary chunking / memory-efficient load (RuWordList redesign), and investigate the other 3 issues. Also re-run release build to measure size; but user aborted. So maybe prioritize user's 4 issues.\n\nLet me write tersely.", "time": {"start": 1791916036326, "end": 1791916044998}, "id": "prt_13684d0e6001vVYYccmwGglQB6", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13684add9001gOhKucbovDh4ck"}, {"type": "text", "text": "## Objective\n- Make Yomikai v2.0.0 installable and fix v2.0.0 UX problems. Root install failure: release APK is 87 MB and the user's device reports 0 allocatable bytes (installd ENOSPC). Primary fix chosen: move the 3M-wordform OCR dictionary out of DEX into a compressed APK asset.\n\n## Important Details\n- Repo: `/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code` — Android app \"Yomikai\" (manga reader + OCR), Kotlin, multi-module Gradle; `applicationId = app.yomikai`, namespace `eu.kanade.tachiyomi`.\n- User writes Russian; answer in Russian.\n- Crash is from the third-party TAPK installer (`ru.trashbox.tapk`), NOT this repo: `java.io.IOException: Failed to allocate 87103556 because only 0 allocatable` at `RootlessSaiPackageInstaller.install` (`session.openWrite`). Means device has ~0 free space to stage the APK.\n- Confirmed: released `yomikai-v2.0.0.apk` size = exactly **87,103,556** bytes (GitHub release sj0404-collab/yomikai v2.0.0). Downloaded to `/tmp/opencode/yomikai-v2.0.0.apk`.\n- Old APK composition: `classes4.dex` (the dictionary DEX) = 140,804,312 bytes uncompressed → **30,163,093** compressed. New asset `assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt` = 71,110,950 → **11,340,327** compressed. Expected saving ≈ 18.8 MB → new release ≈ **68.3 MB** (not yet measured).\n- Dictionary: 3,014,492 unique wordforms, previously hardcoded in 603 files `data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/RuWordListPart*.kt` (~90 MB source). Only `RuWordList.upper` is used; `RuWordList.lower` is dead code.\n- User constraint: **no speed/behavior regression** — \"если ничего по скорости не критично то да а если чтото ухудшиться то не надо\".\n- User-approved approach: plain-text asset in APK (APK zip deflate compresses it automatically; no double gzip, no 3M runtime `uppercase()`).\n- Latest user feedback on v2.0.0 (4 new issues to fix): (1) UI loads very slowly; (2) first OCR call auto-selects models/\"voices\" instead of prompting, heavily slowing the phone; (3) the 3M dictionary must be used in **chunks**, not loaded whole (it hangs hard); (4) manual text-region selection that includes frames/speech bubbles mostly returns no result due to width/length constraints.\n- Debug APK is 103 MB vs release 87 MB — compare release-to-release only. Debug has no R8.\n- App is built arm64-v8a only (`app/build.gradle.kts` splits); `androidResources.noCompress` = `tflite`, `bin` only.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Generated `data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt` (3,014,492 uppercase, sorted, LF, no BOM; 71,110,950 bytes).\n- Rewrote `data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/RuWordList.kt`: `ASSET_PATH=\"ocr/ru_wordlist.txt\"`, `EXPECTED_FORMS=3_014_492`, `TEST_SOURCE_CANDIDATES` (relative paths for JVM tests), `configure(context)`, `openSource()`, `upper: Set<String> by lazy(SYNCHRONIZED)` building `HashSet` with exact capacity, logcat WARN fallback to `emptySet()`.\n- Deleted all 603 `RuWordListPart*.kt`.\n- Wired `mihon.data.ocr.RuWordList.configure(applicationContext)` in `app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/App.kt` (after `OcrVocabulary.configure`, ~lines 148-156).\n- Updated `scripts/gen_ruwordlist.py`: new `write_asset(repo, forms)`; removed `write_parts`, `sync_parts_list`, `repo_forms`, `REPO_OCR_DIR`/`RULIST_KT`/`PART_SIZE`, `import re`; added `ASSET_REL`; `main()` calls `write_asset(repo, forms)`.\n- `gradle.properties`: `kotlin.daemon.jvmargs` back to `-Xmx3g` (was 7g for the 603 files); stale comment removed.\n- Verified: `:data:compileDebugKotlin` OK on 3g; `:data:testDebugUnitTest --tests \"mihon.data.ocr.*\"` all pass (17 classes; `OcrTextCleanerTest` 37/37, `OcrTextCleanerUserDictTest` 8/8) — confirms JVM fallback path resolves; `:app:assembleDebug` OK, asset merged and compressed in APK.\n\n### Active\n- Investigating the 4 new v2.0.0 issues (todos created). 2 of 3 explore tasks returned (startup slowness; OCR engine selection); the manual region-selection explore task was cancelled.\n- Engine-selection facts gathered: registry `data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/OcrPlugins.kt:67`; selection `data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/OcrRepositoryImpl.kt` (`selectedEngineType()`:224, `engineTypeOf()`:233, `engineFor()`:360, `fallbackChain()`:327); pref key `pref_ocr_model` default `OcrModel.CYRILLIC`.\n- Startup facts gathered: heavy main-thread work in `App.kt` (`importModule` ~130, `OcrVocabulary.configure` ~148, `OcrScreenshotBuffer.init` ~160, `initializeMigrator`, `ensureOcrModelsInstalled` ~364).\n\n### Blocked\n- Release APK size NOT measured — user aborted `./gradlew :app:assembleRelease`.\n- `spotlessCheck` NOT run — user aborted `./gradlew :data:spotlessCheck :app:spotlessCheck`.\n- New dictionary design must change: current `RuWordList.upper` still builds the full 3M `HashSet` (memory/hang), which conflicts with user issue (3) \"use in chunks\".\n\n## Next Move\n1. Redesign `RuWordList` for low-memory / chunked or lazy-loading use (e.g. compact `ByteArray` + binary search, or per-first-letter buckets) so it doesn't hang; keep `upper` membership semantics.\n2. Resume/complete the manual region-selection explore task (crop/region path + width/height/aspect acceptance filters in `OcrTextCleaner`, `CyrillicOcrEngine`, `OcrRegionRules`, `OcrBoxGeometry`, `ui/reader|ocr`), then fix issues (1) slow startup, (2) first-run OCR engine chooser, (3) chunked dictionary, (4) manual region rejections.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/RuWordList.kt`: rewritten dictionary loader (asset-based); needs chunked/low-memory rework.\n- `data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt`: new dictionary asset (71,110,950 bytes; compresses to 11,340,327 in APK).\n- `scripts/gen_ruwordlist.py`: generator; now emits the asset (`ASSET_REL`).\n- `app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/App.kt`: startup wiring; `RuWordList.configure` added; heavy main-thread init to audit.\n- `app/build.gradle.kts`: version from `RELEASE_TAG` (fallback 0.8.0), versionCode logic, arm64-v8a split, `noCompress` list.\n- `gradle.properties`: Kotlin daemon heap `-Xmx3g`.\n- `data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/OcrTextCleaner.kt:468`: uses `RuWordList.upper` (dictionary consumer / split logic).\n- `data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/OcrVocabulary.kt:137`: uses `RuWordList.upper`.\n- `data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/OcrRepositoryImpl.kt` + `OcrPlugins.kt`: OCR engine selection/defaults (for issue 2).\n- `data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/OcrRegionRules.kt`, `OcrBoxGeometry.kt`, `CyrillicOcrEngine.kt`: candidates for the manual region width/length filter (issue 4).\n- `app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/tachiyomi/extension/installer/PackageInstallerInstaller.kt`: this repo's own installer (unrelated to the crash).\n- `/tmp/opencode/yomikai-v2.0.0.apk`: pristine released v2.0.0 APK for size/`classes4.dex` comparison.", "time": {"start": 1791916045009, "end": 1791916055467}, "id": "prt_13684f2d10016FsV9nC5z00yer", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13684add9001gOhKucbovDh4ck"}, {"reason": "stop", "snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-finish", "tokens": {"total": 90095, "input": 86518, "output": 2038, "reasoning": 1539, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 0}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_136851e0a001mRiE7ZqAB0LawH", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13684add9001gOhKucbovDh4ck"}]}, {"info": {"role": "user", "time": {"created": 1791916056223}, "agent": "build", "model": {"providerID": "opencode", "modelID": "big-pickle"}, "summary": {"diffs": [{"file": "app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/domain/DomainModule.kt", "patch": "Index: app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/domain/DomainModule.kt\n===================================================================\n--- app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/domain/DomainModule.kt\t\n+++ app/src/main/java/eu/kanade/domain/DomainModule.kt\t\n@@ -1,335 +1,335 @@\n package eu.kanade.domain\n \n import android.app.Application\n import eu.kanade.domain.chapter.interactor.GetAvailableScanlators\n import eu.kanade.domain.chapter.interactor.SetReadStatus\n import eu.kanade.domain.chapter.interactor.SyncChaptersWithSource\n import eu.kanade.domain.download.interactor.DeleteDownload\n import eu.kanade.domain.extension.interactor.GetExtensionLanguages\n import eu.kanade.domain.extension.interactor.GetExtensionSources\n import eu.ka